/* Question bank PA test (English convenience translation), Wft Health Insurance. Vorm: [vraag, [[antwoord, uitleg] x4], toetsterm CDFD]; het EERSTE antwoord is steeds het juiste.
   Gegenereerd met tools/vragen-js.py. */
(window.PA_VRAGEN = window.PA_VRAGEN || {})["zorgverzekering"] = [
["Which facts must an applicant for supplementary health insurance disclose to the insurer under the duty of disclosure?", [["Facts that he knows or ought to know and that he understands to be relevant to acceptance", "That is the standard for the pre-contractual duty of disclosure under the Dutch Civil Code (BW): it concerns facts that may influence the insurer's decision or conditions."], ["All medical data from his GP file, even if it is unrelated to the risk", "The duty of disclosure concerns facts relevant to assessing the risk, not the complete medical file."], ["Only conditions for which he is still receiving treatment at the time of applying", "Earlier conditions may also be relevant if the applicant understands that they influence the insurer's decision."], ["No facts at all, because an obligation to accept applicants applies to all health insurance", "The obligation to accept applicants applies only to basic insurance; for supplementary insurance the insurer may assess the risk."]], "1i.10"],
["What, in broad terms, does the Code of Conduct on the Processing of Personal Data by Health Insurers regulate?", [["How health insurers handle personal data, including health data, with care", "The code of conduct elaborates the privacy rules for health insurers, for example who within the insurer may view medical data."], ["How high the commission may be that health insurers pay to advisers", "Adviser remuneration is not a subject of this privacy code of conduct."], ["Which care health insurers must purchase from which care providers", "Care procurement falls under the duty of care and the supervision of the Dutch Healthcare Authority (NZa), not under this code of conduct."], ["Within what period health insurers must pay out policyholders' claims", "Payment periods for claims are set out in the policy conditions, not in the privacy code of conduct."]], "1a.7"],
["Which description best fits the system of the Health Insurance Act (Zvw)?", [["Private insurers carry out a compulsory insurance within public frameworks", "Health insurance is a private-law contract, but the law determines, among other things, the insurance obligation, the obligation to accept applicants, the package and the premium rules."], ["The government carries out the insurance itself and health insurers only handle the administration", "Health insurers bear the insurance risk themselves and conclude contracts with care providers themselves."], ["Municipalities determine for each resident which health insurance is suitable", "Municipalities implement the Social Support Act (Wmo) and the Youth Act; each insured person chooses their own health insurer."], ["A voluntary insurance whose content is freely determined by each insurer", "The insurance is compulsory and the content of the basic package is laid down by law."]], "1a.1"],
["Who in the Netherlands is required to take out health insurance?", [["Everyone who is insured under the Long-term Care Act (Wlz)", "The insurance obligation is linked to Wlz insurance: residents and non-residents who work here in employment and pay wage tax."], ["Only persons with Dutch nationality", "Nationality is not decisive; a foreigner living here is also subject to the insurance obligation."], ["Only residents with an income above the former sickness fund income limit", "An income limit applied in the past for the sickness fund; under the Zvw income plays no role in the insurance obligation."], ["Only residents aged 18 and over", "Children are also subject to the insurance obligation; they must be registered, but pay no premium."]], "1i.2"],
["Pieter (34) is an engineer and has lived in Canada with his wife and young daughter for the past ten years. On 1 March the family moves back to the Netherlands because Pieter has found a job in Delft. Because of the hectic move, he does not arrange the family's health insurance until early May. He wonders whether his daughter's mid-March doctor's bill is now at his own expense. What applies to the start date of the health insurance if Pieter registers in early May?", [["The insurance starts retroactively on 1 March, the start of the insurance obligation", "Pieter registers within four months; the insurance then applies retroactively to the day the insurance obligation arose. Premium is also due for that period."], ["The insurance does not start until 1 January of the following calendar year, at the annual switching period", "The Zvw has no waiting period until the new year; basic insurance can start at any time during the year."], ["The insurance starts on the day of registration; he pays the March bill himself", "Within the four-month period the insurance in fact applies retroactively to the start of the insurance obligation."], ["The insurer may first have the family medically examined before cover starts", "For basic insurance an obligation to accept applicants applies; medical selection is not permitted."]], "1i.2"],
["Yasmin (27) comes from Morocco and has lived in Utrecht with her Dutch partner since 1 February. She is registered with the municipality, has a residence permit and is taking an integration course. Only in August does she hear from a friend that she must take out health insurance. In the meantime she has seen a doctor twice. What applies if Yasmin registers now, more than six months after her insurance obligation arose?", [["The insurance does not apply retroactively and starts only from the day of registration", "After the four-month period, retroactive effect lapses; Yasmin must bear the healthcare costs from the uninsured period herself."], ["The insurer may refuse her application because the four-month period has expired", "The obligation to accept applicants continues to apply; even a late applicant must be accepted for basic insurance."], ["The insurance nevertheless starts from 1 February, when her insurance obligation arose", "Retroactive effect applies only if registration takes place within four months."], ["She must first wait a year before the basic insurance can start", "There is no waiting period; the insurance starts immediately from registration."]], "1i.2"],
["Lisa (31) and Daan (33) live in Zwolle and have their first child, a son, on 5 March. Lisa is a teacher and Daan works as a self-employed plumber. Both have basic insurance with supplementary dental insurance with the same insurer. In the rush of the maternity week they have not yet thought about their son's insurance. What must they do to ensure that their son is insured from birth?", [["Register their son with a health insurer within four months of the birth", "If registered within four months, the insurance starts retroactively on the date of birth. For a child under 18 no premium is due."], ["Nothing, because their son is automatically co-insured on Lisa's policy", "A child must be registered separately; it is premium-free, but not automatically insured."], ["Register their son before 1 January of the following year", "That period is too generous; after four months the retroactive effect lapses."], ["Take out supplementary insurance for their son with their own health insurer", "The basic insurance must be arranged; supplementary insurance is voluntary and does not replace it."]], "1j.1"],
["Which group is exempt from the insurance obligation of the Health Insurance Act?", [["Military personnel on active service", "Military personnel on active service receive their care through the Ministry of Defence and are therefore not subject to the insurance obligation."], ["Self-employed persons without staff", "A self-employed person without staff who lives here is simply subject to the insurance obligation."], ["Students living in the Netherlands", "Students who live here are also insured under the Wlz and are therefore subject to the insurance obligation."], ["Civil servants employed by central government", "Civil servants have simply fallen under the Zvw since 2006."]], "1i.2"],
["How can someone with conscientious objections to insurance fall outside the insurance obligation of the Zvw?", [["Through an exemption from the Social Insurance Bank (SVB)", "People with conscientious objections can apply to the Social Insurance Bank for a declaration of conscientious objections; they are then not subject to the insurance obligation."], ["Through a statement from the GP that he uses little care", "Use of care plays no role in the insurance obligation."], ["Through written cancellation with his health insurer", "Cancelling without new insurance is not possible as long as the insurance obligation exists."], ["Through applying for an exemption from the Dutch Healthcare Authority", "The NZa is a supervisory authority and does not grant exemptions from the insurance obligation."]], "1c.5"],
["What does the obligation to accept applicants for basic insurance entail?", [["Everyone obliged to insure must be accepted in its operating area", "A health insurer may not refuse an application for basic insurance, regardless of age or health."], ["The insurer may refuse only in the case of a serious chronic condition", "Chronically ill people must also be accepted; that is precisely what the obligation to accept applicants is for."], ["The insured person must accept every offer from his current insurer", "The obligation to accept rests on the insurer, not on the insured person, who may switch every year."], ["The insurer must also always accept the supplementary insurance", "No obligation to accept applicants applies to supplementary insurance."]], "1h.2"],
["Mrs Bakker (62) lives with her husband in Eindhoven and works part-time as an administrative assistant. She has diabetes and rheumatism and therefore regularly visits the hospital. Her current health insurer is raising the premium substantially, so she wants to switch on 1 January. She is afraid that a new insurer will not want her because of her health. What may the new insurer do with her application for basic insurance?", [["Accept her at the same premium as every other insured person with that policy", "Because of the obligation to accept applicants and the ban on premium differentiation, Mrs Bakker is simply accepted at the standard premium."], ["Accept her with a premium surcharge because of her diabetes and rheumatism", "A surcharge based on health is prohibited in basic insurance."], ["Refuse her because she has an increased risk of healthcare costs", "Refusing on grounds of health conflicts with the obligation to accept applicants."], ["Accept her only after she has completed a health declaration", "No medical questions may be asked for basic insurance."]], "1h.2"],
["What does the ban on premium differentiation in basic insurance mean?", [["Everyone with the same policy pays the same premium, regardless of age or health", "The premium may not differ according to personal characteristics such as age, sex or health."], ["All health insurers must charge exactly the same premium", "Insurers set their own premium; it differs per insurer and per policy."], ["The premium may differ only by age category", "Age-related premiums are in fact not permitted in basic insurance."], ["The premium may not be higher than the income-related contribution reimbursed by the employer", "There is no statutory link between the nominal premium and the income-related contribution."]], "1g.5"],
["Which premium discount on basic insurance is permitted?", [["A discount in exchange for a voluntary deductible", "The Zvw permits a premium discount if the insured person opts for a voluntary deductible."], ["A discount for non-smokers and sporty people with a gym membership", "A discount based on lifestyle or health conflicts with the ban on premium differentiation."], ["A discount for young people up to 27", "An age discount is not permitted in basic insurance; in supplementary insurance it is."], ["A discount for insured persons who use no care for a year", "A no-claims discount on basic insurance no longer exists; it was replaced in 2008 by the mandatory deductible."]], "1g.5"],
["A health insurer offers a benefits-in-kind policy and a reimbursement policy. May the premium of those two policies differ?", [["Yes, per policy, but everyone on one policy pays the same", "The ban on premium differentiation applies per product; different policy types may have their own premium."], ["No, an insurer may charge only one premium for basic insurance", "An insurer may offer several basic policies, each with its own premium."], ["Yes, but only if the reimbursement policy covers less care", "The package is identical for all policy types; the difference lies in free choice of doctor and reimbursement."], ["No, the NZa sets the premium for each policy type", "The NZa does not set premiums; insurers determine their own premium."]], "1g.5"],
["What is the purpose of risk equalisation between health insurers?", [["Insurers are compensated for differences in the risk profile of their insured persons", "Because insurers must accept everyone at the same premium, they are compensated for insured persons with higher expected costs."], ["To ensure that all insurers make the same profit", "Risk equalisation corrects for risk differences, not for differences in efficiency or profit."], ["To make the premium per insured person depend on their health and their use of care in the previous year", "That would be premium differentiation, which is prohibited."], ["To distribute defaulters among all health insurers", "A separate scheme for defaulters exists; that is something different from risk equalisation."]], "1a.1"],
["Who determines the content of the basic health insurance package?", [["The government, on the advice of the National Health Care Institute", "The minister lays down the package in regulations; the National Health Care Institute advises on what belongs in it."], ["Each health insurer for its own insured persons", "The basic package is laid down by law and is the same at all insurers."], ["The Dutch Healthcare Authority", "The NZa is responsible for tariffs, performances and supervision, not for the content of the package."], ["The industry association of health insurers", "The industry association represents the interests of insurers, but does not determine the package."]], "1h.1"],
["In what respects can the basic insurance of different health insurers differ from one another?", [["In policy type, contracted care providers, premium and service", "The content of the package is the same; differences lie in freedom of choice of care providers, reimbursement of non-contracted care, premium and service."], ["In the types of care covered by the basic package", "Which care is insured is laid down by law and is the same at all insurers."], ["In the amount of the mandatory deductible", "The mandatory deductible is set by law and is the same for everyone."], ["In the age limit for premium-free insurance of children", "Children under 18 are premium-free at every insurer; this is laid down by law."]], "1d.2"],
["Which care falls under the basic package of the Health Insurance Act?", [["District nursing", "Nursing and care at home by the district nurse has fallen under the Zvw since 2015."], ["Domestic help", "Domestic support is a customised service provided by the municipality under the Wmo."], ["A routine dental check-up for an adult", "Regular dental care for adults is not in the basic package, but can be insured as supplementary cover."], ["Repatriation after an accident abroad", "Transport back to the Netherlands is not covered by basic insurance; travel insurance or supplementary insurance is needed for that."]], "1d.1"],
["Joost (35) is an account manager in Amersfoort, married and the father of two children. He is training for a half marathon and sprains his ankle while running. On his GP's advice he goes to the physiotherapist six times. Joost has no chronic condition and only basic insurance. How are these treatments reimbursed?", [["Not from basic insurance; he pays for them himself", "Physiotherapy for adults is included in the basic package only in limited cases, such as certain chronic conditions. An ankle injury does not fall under this."], ["In full from basic insurance, because the GP advised it", "A recommendation or referral from the GP does not make this physiotherapy basic care for an adult."], ["From basic insurance, outside the mandatory deductible", "This physiotherapy is not basic care and therefore not an exception to the deductible either."], ["Through the municipality's Wmo, because it concerns restoring mobility", "The Wmo does not reimburse physiotherapy; it falls under the Zvw or supplementary insurance."]], "1g.2"],
["By which criteria does the National Health Care Institute assess whether care belongs in the basic package?", [["Effectiveness, cost-effectiveness, necessity and feasibility", "These are the four package criteria that the National Health Care Institute applies in its advice on the basic package."], ["Popularity, availability, price and waiting time", "Popularity and waiting time are not package criteria."], ["Age, income, health and place of residence of the patient", "These are personal characteristics; the package is the same for everyone."], ["Profitability, market share, solvency and costs of the health insurer", "These are business-economic measures of insurers, not package criteria."]], "1h.1"],
["What is the general condition that care must meet in order to be reimbursed from basic insurance?", [["The care must meet the state of science and practice", "Care is insured only if it is proven effective; experimental care generally falls outside the package."], ["The care must have been prescribed by a medical specialist", "Much basic care, such as GP care, does not require a specialist's prescription."], ["The care must be provided in the Netherlands", "Care abroad can also be reimbursed under certain conditions."], ["The care must be cheaper than any comparable alternative treatment", "Cost-effectiveness plays a role in package decisions, but is not a condition assessed for each claim."]], "1i.2"],
["What does a health insurer's preferential policy for medicines mean?", [["For each active substance only the designated medicine is reimbursed, except in cases of medical necessity", "Where the prescriber indicates medical necessity, the insurer must nevertheless reimburse the other medicine."], ["The insured person may choose any brand-name medicine without paying extra, provided the GP prescribes it", "Preferential policy in fact restricts the choice to the designated medicine."], ["The pharmacist determines which medicine is included in the package", "The package is determined by the government; within that package the insurer designates the preferred medicine."], ["Medicines fall only under supplementary insurance, not under basic insurance", "Registered medicines that have been designated fall under the basic package."]], "1l.1"],
["What is the difference between a co-payment and the deductible?", [["A co-payment belongs to a specific type of care; the deductible applies to healthcare costs per year", "A co-payment, such as for maternity care or certain aids, is also paid when the deductible has already been used up."], ["A co-payment applies only to supplementary insurance, the deductible only to basic insurance", "Co-payments also exist within basic insurance, for example for medicines above the reimbursement limit."], ["There is no difference; both terms are used interchangeably in the policy conditions", "They are different schemes, each with its own operation."], ["The deductible applies only to children under 18", "The mandatory deductible in fact does not apply to children under 18."]], "1d.8"],
["For whom does the mandatory deductible of health insurance apply?", [["For insured persons aged 18 and over", "Children under 18 have no deductible; from age 18 the mandatory deductible applies."], ["For all insured persons, including children", "For children under 18 no deductible applies."], ["Only for insured persons with a reimbursement policy", "The mandatory deductible applies to every policy type."], ["Only for insured persons with an income above a statutory limit", "The deductible is not income-related."]], "1d.8"],
["Which care is NOT subject to the mandatory deductible?", [["GP care", "GP care is exempted by law from the deductible, so that the threshold for visiting the GP remains low."], ["Treatment by a medical specialist in hospital", "Medical specialist care falls under the deductible."], ["Treatment in specialised mental healthcare", "Mental healthcare treatments in basic insurance fall under the deductible."], ["Ambulance transport to the hospital", "Patient transport falls under the deductible."]], "1g.2"],
["Which costs DO count towards the mandatory deductible?", [["Medicines prescribed by the GP", "The GP consultation is exempted, but prescribed medicines do fall under the deductible."], ["A consultation with the GP", "GP care is exempted from the deductible."], ["Obstetric care and maternity care after a home birth", "Obstetrics and maternity care are exempted; a co-payment does apply for maternity care."], ["District nursing at someone's home", "District nursing falls outside the deductible."]], "1g.2"],
["What is the gist of the Covenant on the overlap between travel insurance and health insurance?", [["Agreements on handling medical costs abroad when both insurances provide cover", "The covenant prevents the insured person from being caught between two insurers; the insurers arrange the division of costs among themselves."], ["A ban on travel insurers reimbursing medical costs abroad", "Travel insurance may cover medical costs; the covenant is precisely about the overlap of the two covers."], ["An obligation for every insured person to take out travel insurance in addition to health insurance", "Travel insurance is voluntary; the covenant imposes no obligation on insured persons."], ["An agreement that the travel insurer always pays everything and the health insurer never does", "Health insurance continues to cover care abroad; the covenant regulates how the insurers settle up together."]], "1a.8"],
["Emma lives with her parents in Groningen and is in the final year of pre-university education (vwo). She turns 18 on 14 June and will then pay the premium for her basic insurance herself. She has asthma and expects to visit the lung specialist in hospital a few more times this year. Her mother asks the adviser how the deductible will work out for Emma. How does the mandatory deductible work for Emma in the calendar year of her 18th birthday?", [["The deductible applies pro rata from 1 July", "The deductible starts on the first day of the month after the 18th birthday and is calculated proportionally for that year."], ["The full deductible applies for the whole year", "For the months before her 18th birthday, no deductible applies to Emma."], ["The deductible applies only from 1 January of the following year", "The deductible already starts in the year of the 18th birthday, pro rata."], ["The deductible applies from 14 June, her birthday", "Premium and deductible start on the first day of the month after the birthday, not on the birthday itself."]], "1d.8"],
["What is a voluntary deductible?", [["An additional deductible on top of the mandatory one, in exchange for a lower premium", "The insured person chooses it voluntarily and receives a premium discount for it; it applies to the same care as the mandatory deductible."], ["A deductible that applies only to the supplementary insurance", "The voluntary deductible belongs to basic insurance."], ["A deductible that replaces the mandatory deductible, in exchange for a lower premium", "The voluntary deductible comes on top and does not replace the mandatory part."], ["A deductible that also applies to GP care", "The voluntary deductible has the same exceptions as the mandatory one, so GP care remains outside it."]], "1d.8"],
["How high can the voluntary deductible in basic insurance be?", [["In steps of €100 up to a maximum of €500 on top of the mandatory deductible", "The Zvw permits a voluntary deductible of €100, €200, €300, €400 or €500."], ["Any amount that the insured person and the insurer agree together", "The law determines the possible steps; free negotiation is not permitted."], ["At most the amount of one annual premium", "The maximum is not an annual premium, but a fixed amount of €500."], ["In steps of €250 up to a maximum of €1,000 on top of the mandatory deductible", "The Zvw has no such steps; the maximum is €500."]], "1d.8"],
["Mr Smit (66) is retired and lives with his wife in Apeldoorn. He has COPD and sees the lung specialist several times a year, sometimes with a hospital admission. His healthcare costs are well above the mandatory deductible every year. To save premium, he is considering taking the maximum voluntary deductible. What is the right advice?", [["Advise against it, because he will almost certainly pay the additional deductible in full", "With predictably high healthcare costs, the additional out-of-pocket payment is usually greater than the premium discount he receives."], ["Recommend it, because chronically ill people receive a higher premium discount", "The discount is the same for everyone with the same voluntary deductible; health plays no role."], ["Recommend it, because hospital care for chronically ill people falls outside the deductible", "Hospital care simply falls under the deductible; only chain care, for example, is exempted."], ["Advise against it, because chronically ill people are by law not allowed to choose a voluntary deductible", "Every insured person aged 18 or over may choose; for Mr Smit it is merely unfavourable."]], "2e.6"],
["Ilse (45) is a nurse in Leiden and the mother of a teenage son. On 10 December a treatment pathway for her knee problems starts at the hospital, continuing into March of the following year. She has already largely used up her deductible for the current year. She hopes she will not have to pay again for this pathway next year. Against the deductible of which year do the costs of this pathway count?", [["The year in which the pathway started", "For medical specialist care, the start date of the care pathway counts for the deductible; for Ilse that is therefore the current year."], ["The year in which the pathway ends", "The end date matters for the claim, but not for the year of the deductible."], ["Divided pro rata over both years", "The costs of one pathway are not split over two years."], ["The year in which the insurer pays the invoice", "The moment of payment is not decisive for the deductible."]], "1l.4"],
["What characterises a benefits-in-kind policy?", [["The insured person is entitled to care from providers contracted by the insurer", "With benefits in kind, the insurer provides the care through contracted providers; non-contracted care is often reimbursed at a lower rate."], ["The insured person freely chooses a care provider and always has the costs reimbursed in full", "That fits a reimbursement policy, and even then a maximum at a market-conform level applies."], ["The insured person pays for all care himself and claims afterwards", "With benefits in kind, the contracted provider generally bills the insurer directly."], ["The policy covers fewer types of care than a reimbursement policy", "The package is the same for every policy type; the difference lies in freedom of choice."]], "1d.6"],
["What characterises a reimbursement policy?", [["The insured person is entitled to reimbursement of healthcare costs at a care provider of his choice", "With reimbursement, the insured person chooses freely and the insurer reimburses up to a market-conform or statutory tariff."], ["The insured person may only go to care providers with whom the insurer has concluded a contract", "That is a characteristic of benefits-in-kind and budget policies."], ["The insured person pays no deductible", "The mandatory deductible also applies with reimbursement."], ["The insured person has dental care and physiotherapy reimbursed in addition to basic care", "The policy type does not change the content of the package."]], "1d.6"],
["How much must a health insurer at minimum reimburse under a benefits-in-kind policy for care from a non-contracted care provider?", [["Enough that the reimbursement does not form a practical obstacle to that choice", "According to the Zvw (art. 13) and case law, the insurer may reduce the reimbursement, but not so far that free choice becomes practically impossible."], ["Always the full amount of the invoice", "Full reimbursement of non-contracted care is not mandatory with benefits in kind."], ["Nothing, because with a benefits-in-kind policy the insured person is entitled only to contracted care", "A reimbursement of zero would form an obstacle and is therefore not permitted."], ["The same amount as under a reimbursement policy", "A reimbursement policy generally reimburses more; with benefits in kind the reimbursement may be lower."]], "1d.6"],
["What is a combination policy?", [["A policy with benefits in kind for some types of care and reimbursement for others", "A combination policy mixes both forms, for example free choice for hospital care and benefits in kind for other care."], ["A basic insurance and a supplementary insurance in one package with one insurer", "That is a combination of insurances, not a policy type of basic insurance."], ["A policy that partners take out together", "Whether partners are on one policy says nothing about the policy type."], ["A policy that covers both the Zvw and the Wlz", "The Wlz is a national insurance scheme and is not covered through a health policy."]], "1d.6"],
["What characterises a budget policy?", [["A benefits-in-kind policy with few contracted care providers and a lower premium", "Anyone who goes to a non-contracted provider often receives a lower reimbursement under a budget policy."], ["A policy with a smaller basic package, which makes the premium lower", "A budget policy also covers the full statutory basic package."], ["A policy without a mandatory deductible", "The mandatory deductible applies to every policy."], ["A policy available only to people on a minimum income through the municipality, with a lower premium", "A budget policy is open to everyone; for people on a minimum income, municipal group schemes exist in addition."]], "1d.6"],
["Mrs Visser (52) is a lawyer in The Hague and has suffered from a herniated disc for years. She wants to be operated on by a specialist at a private clinic with which her current insurer has no contract. She currently has a benefits-in-kind policy and wants to change policy on 1 January. She wants to pay as little as possible herself for the operation. Which policy type best fits her wish?", [["A reimbursement policy", "A reimbursement policy reimburses care from a provider of choice up to a market-conform tariff, even without a contract with the clinic."], ["A budget policy", "A budget policy has few contracts and often reimburses non-contracted care at a lower rate."], ["A benefits-in-kind policy", "With benefits in kind she generally receives a lower reimbursement for non-contracted care."], ["A policy with a voluntary deductible", "A voluntary deductible lowers the premium, but increases her own payment."]], "2e.4"],
["Mr Jansen (59) is the director of a transport company and has a reimbursement policy. He has hip surgery at a non-contracted private clinic. The clinic charges a tariff well above the tariff customary in the Netherlands. He submits the full invoice to his health insurer. What applies to the reimbursement?", [["Up to the market-conform tariff; he pays the excess himself", "Even with reimbursement, the insurer reimburses no more than a reasonable tariff, customary in the Netherlands or set by law."], ["The insurer must reimburse the full amount claimed", "Reimbursement means free choice of care provider, not unlimited reimbursement of any tariff."], ["The insurer reimburses nothing, because the clinic has no contract", "With reimbursement, a contract with the clinic is not needed for reimbursement."], ["The additional costs are charged to his mandatory deductible", "The deductible applies to insured costs; costs above the reimbursable tariff are not insured at all."]], "1l.4"],
["When can an insured person generally switch to another basic insurance?", [["Once a year, on 1 January", "Basic insurance can be cancelled annually with effect from 1 January; mid-year this is possible only in special situations."], ["At any time, with a notice period of one month", "Free mid-year cancellation is not possible with basic insurance."], ["Only if the premium rises by more than ten per cent", "A premium increase does not give a separate cancellation moment in the middle of the year; switching is simply possible on 1 January."], ["Once every three years, after the contract term has ended", "The Zvw has no multi-year contracts for basic insurance."]], "1k.1"],
["Karin (38) is single, works as a marketing manager in Rotterdam and exercises a lot. In mid-November she sees that her health insurer is raising the premium for next year. She wants to switch on 1 January to a cheaper benefits-in-kind policy with another insurer. Because of the holidays she does not get round to it until the end of December. Which deadlines apply to her switch?", [["Cancel by 31 December at the latest; the new policy can be concluded up to and including 31 January, with effect from 1 January", "Karin can cancel until the end of the year and still has time in January to conclude a new policy, without being uninsured."], ["Cancel by 1 November at the latest; the new insurance must be concluded before 1 December and then starts on 1 January", "Such early deadlines do not apply; cancellation is possible until the end of the year."], ["Cancel by 31 January at the latest; the new insurance then starts on 1 March", "Too late: cancellation must take place before 1 January, and the new insurance applies retroactively to 1 January."], ["Cancel by 30 November at the latest; the new insurance starts on the day it is concluded, without retroactive effect", "The law allows cancellation up to and including 31 December, with retroactive effect for the new policy."]], "1a.5"],
["What does the cancellation service involve when switching health insurer?", [["The new insurer cancels the old insurance on his behalf", "With the cancellation service the insured person does not have to cancel himself; this prevents him from being double-insured or uninsured."], ["The old insurer looks for a new insurer for the insured person", "The old insurer does not refer customers to a competitor."], ["The CAK arranges the switch for all insured persons", "The CAK plays no role in ordinary switches."], ["The adviser is obliged to send the cancellation by registered post", "No registered cancellation is needed; the new insurer arranges it."]], "1k.4"],
["Ronald (41) was unemployed for several months after his employer went bankrupt. During that period a premium arrear arose with his health insurer. He now has a new job and wants to switch to a cheaper insurer on 1 January. He cancels his insurance in December without paying the arrears. What may his current health insurer do?", [["Refuse the cancellation as long as the arrears have not been paid", "An insurer may refuse the cancellation in the case of a premium arrear; this prevents a defaulter from repeatedly switching and leaving debts behind."], ["Terminate Ronald's basic insurance with immediate effect", "The insurer may not leave the insured person uninsured; the defaulters scheme exists for that."], ["Oblige the new insurer to take over the full debt", "The new insurer does not take over premium debt from the old insurer."], ["Set off the arrears against his healthcare allowance itself", "A health insurer cannot itself set off against the healthcare allowance."]], "1k.2"],
["In which situation does basic insurance end in the middle of the year?", [["When the insured person emigrates and is no longer obliged to insure", "When the insurance obligation ends, the basic insurance can end mid-year."], ["When the insured person moves within the Netherlands", "A move within the Netherlands does not affect the insurance obligation."], ["When the mandatory deductible has been used up in full", "Using up the deductible has no effect on the term."], ["When the insured person is dissatisfied with customer service and reports it in writing", "Dissatisfaction is not a ground for cancelling mid-year; switching is possible on 1 January."]], "1k.1"],
["Which rule applies to supplementary health insurance?", [["No obligation to accept applies; the insurer may refuse", "The obligation to accept applicants under the Zvw applies only to basic insurance."], ["The same obligation to accept applicants applies as for basic insurance", "Supplementary insurance is not covered by the obligation to accept applicants."], ["The premium must be the same for everyone", "The ban on premium differentiation applies only to basic insurance."], ["The cover is determined annually by the National Health Care Institute", "The content of supplementary insurance is determined by the insurer itself."]], "1h.2"],
["May a health insurer ask medical questions when someone applies for supplementary insurance?", [["Yes, it may; it may refuse or restrict the application on that basis", "With supplementary insurance the insurer may assess the risk, for example by means of a health declaration."], ["No, medical questions are prohibited for all health insurance", "The ban on medical selection applies only to basic insurance."], ["Only if the applicant is older than 65", "There is no statutory age limit for asking medical questions."], ["Only with the permission of the NZa", "No permission from the NZa is needed for a health declaration."]], "1d.7"],
["What is a waiting period in supplementary insurance?", [["An initial period in which certain care is not yet reimbursed", "Waiting periods occur mainly with extensive dental cover and orthodontics."], ["The statutory period within which the insurer must pay a claim", "A payment period is something different from a waiting period in the cover."], ["The maximum waiting time for treatment by a contracted provider", "Those are the so-called Treeknormen (maximum waiting times), which belong to the duty of care in basic insurance."], ["The period within which the insured person must cancel", "A notice period has nothing to do with a waiting period for reimbursement."]], "1d.4"],
["May a health insurer make the premium of a supplementary insurance dependent on the age of the insured person?", [["Yes, for supplementary insurance the premium may differ by age", "The ban on premium differentiation applies only to basic insurance."], ["No, the premium must be the same for all ages", "That rule applies to basic insurance, not to supplementary insurance."], ["Only for insured persons younger than 18", "There is no statutory restriction to children."], ["Only if the NZa has approved the premium difference per age group in advance", "The NZa does not approve premiums for supplementary insurance."]], "1g.5"],
["Can an insured person take out their basic insurance with one insurer and their supplementary insurance with another?", [["Yes, but not every insurer offers supplementary insurance separately", "The law does not prohibit it, but insurers may require that the basic insurance is also with them."], ["No, the law requires both insurances with the same insurer", "There is no statutory obligation to have both with one insurer."], ["Yes, and the insurer of the supplementary insurance must then always accept him", "No obligation to accept applicants applies to supplementary insurance."], ["No, supplementary insurance is possible only within a group scheme", "Supplementary insurance can also be taken out individually."]], "1d.4"],
["Mr De Vries (58) is a teacher and has a bad back and an artificial knee. He has extensive supplementary insurance with a lot of physiotherapy. He wants to switch his basic insurance to an insurer with a lower premium. With his current insurer, the supplementary insurance is available only together with the basic insurance. What is careful advice?", [["Cancel only once it is certain that a new insurer will accept him for comparable supplementary cover", "Without an obligation to accept applicants for supplementary insurance, Mr De Vries, given his health, risks losing his supplementary cover."], ["Cancel immediately, because the new insurer must also accept him for supplementary insurance under the obligation to accept applicants", "The obligation to accept applicants applies only to basic insurance."], ["Cancel and from now on have the costs of physiotherapy reimbursed via the healthcare allowance", "The healthcare allowance is a contribution towards the premium, not a replacement for supplementary insurance."], ["Do not switch, because above the age of 55 switching supplementary insurance is restricted by law", "There is no statutory age limit for switching; the risk lies in acceptance for the supplementary insurance."]], "3d.2"],
["Which dental care for an adult falls under basic insurance?", [["Oral surgery and a full removable denture", "For adults, basic insurance covers, among other things, oral surgery and the full denture, for which a co-payment may apply."], ["The six-monthly check-up and teeth cleaning at the dentist", "Regular check-ups for adults do not fall under basic insurance."], ["Filling cavities", "Ordinary dental treatments for adults are not covered by basic insurance."], ["A crown or bridge after tooth loss", "Crowns and bridges generally do not fall under basic insurance for adults."]], "1d.1"],
["How is dental care for children under 18 arranged in basic insurance?", [["Regular dental care, such as check-ups and fillings, falls under basic insurance", "For children under 18, basic insurance covers ordinary dental care."], ["Dental care for children is provided through the municipality's Youth Act", "The Youth Act concerns youth care, not dental care."], ["Dental care for children falls only under supplementary insurance", "Ordinary dental care for children is in fact in the basic package."], ["Only emergency dental care falls under basic insurance", "Check-ups and preventive care are also covered by basic insurance for children."]], "1d.1"],
["Sem (11) lives with his parents and sister in Arnhem and is in the final year of primary school (groep 8). The dentist sees that his teeth are crooked and refers him to the orthodontist. There is no question of a very severe developmental disorder of the teeth. His parents want to know what the braces will cost. How are Sem's braces reimbursed?", [["Not from basic insurance; supplementary insurance may cover orthodontics", "Orthodontics is in the basic package only for very severe abnormalities; for Sem, supplementary insurance is needed."], ["From basic insurance, because dental care for children under 18 is always insured", "Basic insurance covers regular dental care for children, but orthodontics only in exceptional situations."], ["Through the municipality, under the Wmo", "The Wmo does not reimburse dental care."], ["From basic insurance, but with a deductible for his parents", "Children have no deductible, and orthodontics is not basic care here."]], "1g.2"],
["Anouk (42) is a hairdresser in Haarlem and the mother of three children. Her wisdom teeth keep causing infections. The dentist refers her to an oral surgeon at the hospital, who removes the teeth surgically. Anouk has no supplementary dental insurance. How are the costs of the oral surgeon reimbursed?", [["From basic insurance, with the mandatory deductible applying", "Oral surgery is care covered by basic insurance and falls under the deductible."], ["From basic insurance, without a deductible", "Oral surgery is not exempted from the deductible."], ["Not at all, because she has no supplementary dental insurance", "Oral surgery is in the basic package; no supplementary insurance is needed for it."], ["Not at all, because dental care for adults is never reimbursed", "Certain dental care for adults, such as oral surgery, does fall under basic insurance."]], "1g.2"],
["What applies to the content of a basic insurance taken out through a group scheme?", [["The basic package is the same as that of an individual basic insurance", "A group scheme may have other conditions or additional arrangements, but the statutory basic package remains the same."], ["The group scheme may remove types of care from the basic package", "The basic package is laid down by law and cannot be restricted."], ["The mandatory deductible lapses for participants in a group scheme", "The mandatory deductible also applies within a group scheme."], ["Members of the group scheme are medically examined", "Medical selection is always prohibited for basic insurance."]], "1b.3"],
["What is a municipal group health insurance scheme (gemeentepolis)?", [["A group scheme that municipalities offer to residents on a low income", "In this way municipalities offer people on a minimum income health insurance with suitable supplementary cover, sometimes with a contribution from the municipality."], ["A compulsory insurance for all residents of a municipality", "Participation is voluntary and aimed at residents on a low income."], ["An insurance that replaces Wmo services", "The Wmo remains a municipal service alongside health insurance."], ["A policy under which the municipality itself carries out the basic insurance and collects the premium", "The insurance is carried out by a health insurer; the municipality concludes the group contract."]], "1b.3"],
["Hamza (29) is an IT specialist and takes part in a group health insurance scheme through his employer. He lives with his girlfriend and has supplementary insurance with physiotherapy because of an old knee injury. On 1 May he starts working for a different employer, which does not offer a group scheme. He wonders whether he now has to take out new basic insurance. What happens to his basic insurance?", [["The basic insurance continues; only the group benefits may lapse", "The end of employment does not end the insurance; the insurer generally continues the policy on an individual basis."], ["The basic insurance ends on his last working day with the old employer", "Hamza remains subject to the insurance obligation and insured; the policy does not end because the employment ends."], ["His old employer must continue paying the premium until 1 January", "The employer is not obliged to continue paying premium."], ["He must be accepted again after a medical examination", "Medical selection for basic insurance is prohibited."]], "1j.2"],
["From which two main sources is basic insurance financed?", [["The nominal premium and the income-related contribution under the Zvw", "Insured persons aged 18 and over pay premium to their insurer; in addition, an income-related contribution is due on income."], ["The healthcare allowance and the Wlz co-payment", "The healthcare allowance is a contribution for insured persons and the Wlz is a separate national insurance scheme."], ["The national insurance contributions and the employee insurance contributions through payroll tax", "Those are contributions for, among others, AOW (state pension), the Wlz and unemployment benefit (WW), not for the Zvw."], ["Municipal taxes and the central government Wmo contribution", "The Wmo is financed through municipalities and is separate from health insurance."]], "1g.5"],
["Who pays the income-related contribution under the Zvw on an employee's wages?", [["The employer, through the employer's levy under the Zvw", "Since 2013 the employer has paid the employer's levy on the employee's wages; the employee does not pay this contribution himself."], ["The employee, through an assessment from the health insurer", "Health insurers collect only the nominal premium, not the income-related contribution."], ["The employee, after which the employer gives a taxed reimbursement", "That old reimbursement system was replaced in 2013 by the employer's levy."], ["The UWV, on the basis of the payroll records", "The UWV pays no contribution on the wages of employees working for an employer."]], "1g.4"],
["Sophie (36) has her own design studio and works as a self-employed person without staff. She is married, has two young children and is healthy. Her husband is an employee. She asks her adviser why her tax assessment shows a Zvw contribution when she already pays her premium to the health insurer. How does Sophie pay the income-related Zvw contribution on her profit?", [["Herself, at the lower rate, through an assessment from the Tax Administration", "Entrepreneurs and others without an employer pay the contribution themselves at a lower rate, following an assessment based on their income. This is separate from the nominal premium."], ["Through her health insurer, on top of the nominal premium, as a fixed percentage of the profit", "The health insurer does not collect the income-related contribution."], ["Not at all, because self-employed persons are exempt from the contribution", "The contribution is also due on profit from business."], ["Through her husband's employer's levy, at the high rate", "The employer's levy applies to wages, not to a self-employed person's profit."]], "1g.4"],
["What applies to the income-related Zvw contribution in the case of a high income?", [["The contribution is levied up to a maximum contribution income, not above it", "A maximum contribution income applies, so that the contribution does not rise without limit as income rises."], ["The percentage rises progressively with income, just like the brackets in box 1", "Fixed percentages apply, not progressive brackets."], ["Above a certain income the insurance obligation lapses", "The insurance obligation is independent of income."], ["With a high income one no longer pays a nominal premium", "Everyone aged 18 and over pays the nominal premium to their insurer."]], "1g.4"],
["How is care for children under 18 financed in basic insurance, given that they pay no premium?", [["Through a state contribution to the Health Insurance Fund", "Central government pays a contribution to the Health Insurance Fund for the premium-free insurance of children."], ["Through a higher premium for the parents who co-insure them", "Parents pay no extra premium for their children."], ["Through the SVB child benefit", "Child benefit is a national insurance scheme and is not used to pay health premiums."], ["Through the parents' healthcare allowance", "The healthcare allowance is a contribution towards adults' own premium."]], "1g.5"],
["Which conditions, among others, must someone meet to be entitled to the healthcare allowance?", [["Be of legal age, have Dutch health insurance and stay below the income and assets limits", "The healthcare allowance is an income-related contribution for adult insured persons; lawful residence is also a condition."], ["Have supplementary insurance and earn less than a modal income, regardless of own assets", "Supplementary insurance is not a condition; it concerns the basic insurance."], ["Have a benefits-in-kind policy with a contracted health insurer", "The policy type plays no role in entitlement to the healthcare allowance."], ["Have at least one child and pay rent", "These are not conditions for the healthcare allowance; they apply in part to other allowances."]], "1g.6"],
["Jesse (26) has just graduated and works as a junior researcher in Utrecht on a modest salary. He lives alone and receives the healthcare allowance. Because he wants to choose freely which psychologist treats him, he is considering a more expensive reimbursement policy. He hopes his healthcare allowance will then rise too. Does the choice of the more expensive reimbursement policy affect the amount of his healthcare allowance?", [["No, the healthcare allowance is based on a standard premium, not on his own premium", "The allowance is based on a statutory standard premium; Jesse's choice of policy or premium has no influence."], ["Yes, the higher the premium, the higher the healthcare allowance, up to a statutory maximum", "An expensive policy would then automatically give more allowance; the scheme does not work that way."], ["Yes, because with a reimbursement policy the entitlement to healthcare allowance lapses", "The policy type is not relevant to entitlement to the healthcare allowance."], ["No, but his insurer must compensate the premium difference with the benefits-in-kind policy", "There is no compensation obligation for the insurer."]], "1g.6"],
["Which income counts as the assessment income for the healthcare allowance?", [["Generally the collective income, plus any allowance partner's", "The General Act on Income-Related Schemes (AWIR) uses the collective income of the applicant and his allowance partner."], ["The applicant's net monthly wage", "The AWIR uses the annual taxable income, not the net monthly wage."], ["Only the applicant's income, never that of a fiscal partner or allowance partner", "The income of an allowance partner counts."], ["The income of the year in which the application is submitted", "What counts is the income of the year for which the allowance is awarded, not the year of application."]], "1g.6"],
["Fatima (33) is a single mother and works part-time in home care. She receives the healthcare allowance as an advance based on an estimated annual income. During the year she starts working more hours, but forgets to report this. Afterwards her income turns out to be clearly higher than estimated. What happens to her healthcare allowance?", [["In the final calculation, the advance received in excess is reclaimed", "An advance is provisional; once the income has been determined, the final calculation follows and, where necessary, recovery."], ["Nothing, because an advance once paid out is final", "An advance is by definition provisional."], ["Her health insurer offsets the difference against her premium", "The health insurer is not involved in determining or recovering the healthcare allowance."], ["She receives a fine and loses the right to the healthcare allowance for five years", "A higher income leads to recovery, not to an automatic fine or exclusion."]], "1g.6"],
["Until when can someone apply for the healthcare allowance for a given calendar year?", [["Up to and including 1 September of the following year", "The AWIR allows applications after the event up to 1 September of the following year."], ["By 1 January of the year in question at the latest", "Applying is also possible during and after the end of the year."], ["Up to five years after the end of the year", "The application period is not that long."], ["Only within four months of taking out the health insurance", "The four-month period belongs to the insurance obligation, not to the healthcare allowance."]], "1g.6"],
["What is the gist of the recourse covenant between health insurers and liability insurers?", [["Agreements to settle the recovery of healthcare costs from liability insurers in a simple way", "Health insurers have a right of recourse when a third party is liable; the covenant allows a simpler settlement than an extensive assessment in each case."], ["An agreement that health insurers never recover healthcare costs from a liable third party", "The right of recourse remains; the covenant regulates precisely how that recourse is settled."], ["A scheme under which the insured person must reclaim the healthcare costs himself from the liable party", "Recourse is exercised by the health insurer, not by the insured person."], ["Agreements on the premium that liability insurers pay to health insurers", "The covenant concerns recovery of healthcare costs incurred, not premiums between insurers."]], "1a.8"],
["For whom is the Long-term Care Act (Wlz) intended?", [["For people who permanently need constant supervision or 24-hour care nearby", "The Wlz is aimed at heavy, long-term care, for example in the case of severe dementia or a severe disability."], ["For anyone who temporarily needs domestic help or support with day activities", "Domestic help falls under the municipality's Wmo."], ["For people recovering for a short time after a hospital admission", "Short-term care after an admission generally falls under the Zvw."], ["For young people under 18 with psychological problems", "Youth care, including youth mental healthcare, falls under the Youth Act."]], "1i.1"],
["Which body determines whether someone has access to care under the Wlz?", [["The Care Needs Assessment Centre (CIZ)", "The CIZ assesses whether someone meets the access criteria of the Wlz and issues an assessment decision."], ["The client's health insurer", "The health insurer implements the Zvw, not access to the Wlz."], ["The municipality, through a kitchen table conversation", "A kitchen table conversation belongs to the Wmo."], ["The GP, with a referral", "A referral from the GP does not give access to the Wlz."]], "1i.1"],
["Mrs Peters (81) is a widow and lives independently in a terraced house in Deventer. After a fall she has had a hip operation and is now returning home. In the coming weeks she needs help with washing and dressing and with keeping her house clean. Her daughter lives far away and cannot help every day. How is this help generally arranged?", [["Washing and dressing via district nursing (Zvw), cleaning via the Wmo", "Personal care by district nursing is Zvw care; domestic help is a Wmo service provided by the municipality."], ["Both through the Wlz, because she is older than 80", "Age is not decisive; the Wlz requires a permanent need for constant supervision."], ["Both through the municipality's Wmo, in one customised service at home", "Personal care by district nursing falls under the Zvw, not under the Wmo."], ["Both through supplementary insurance, home care component", "District nursing is care covered by basic insurance and domestic help is a municipal service."]], "1i.1"],
["Which organisation collects the co-payment for Wlz care and for customised Wmo services?", [["The CAK", "The CAK calculates and collects the co-payments for both the Wlz and the Wmo."], ["The health insurer", "The health insurer collects the premium and the deductible under the Zvw, not the Wlz or Wmo co-payment."], ["The Benefits Administration (Dienst Toeslagen)", "The Benefits Administration pays out allowances and does not collect co-payments."], ["The National Health Care Institute", "The National Health Care Institute advises on the package and manages funds, but does not collect co-payments."]], "1a.3"],
["Wim (68) is a retired carpenter and lives independently with his wife in an apartment. Because of a muscle disease he can walk less and less well. He now needs a wheelchair for daily use in and around the home. He has no Wlz assessment. Where can Wim generally turn for this wheelchair?", [["The municipality, under the Wmo", "Wheelchairs for daily use are provided under the Wmo for people living independently."], ["His health insurer, under the basic insurance", "A wheelchair for daily use does not fall under the Zvw in this situation."], ["The CIZ, which provides the wheelchair", "The CIZ assesses for the Wlz, but does not provide aids."], ["The UWV, as a provision for incapacity for work", "The UWV provides only provisions related to work, and Wim is retired."]], "1i.1"],
["Under which law does mental healthcare for young people under 18 fall?", [["The Youth Act, carried out by the municipality", "Since 2015 the municipality has been responsible for youth care, including youth mental healthcare."], ["The Health Insurance Act, carried out by the health insurer", "Mental healthcare for adults falls under the Zvw; for young people under 18 the Youth Act applies."], ["The Long-term Care Act, carried out by the care office", "The Wlz is for permanent heavy care, not for regular youth mental healthcare."], ["The Wmo 2015, carried out by the municipality", "The Wmo concerns social support; youth care for minors falls under the Youth Act."]], "1i.1"],
["What is the European Health Insurance Card (EHIC) used for?", [["For medically necessary care during a temporary stay in another EU/EEA country or Switzerland", "With the EHIC the insured person receives care under the rules and tariffs of the public system of the country of stay."], ["For planned treatments in any country in the world", "The EHIC applies only in the EU, the EEA and Switzerland and is intended for unforeseen, medically necessary care."], ["For repatriation to the Netherlands after an accident", "Transport back is not covered by the EHIC, nor by basic insurance."], ["As a replacement for travel insurance, including cover for luggage, cancellation and repatriation", "The EHIC covers only healthcare costs, not luggage or cancellation."]], "1g.7"],
["The Mulder family, two parents and three children from Ede, are touring Thailand. The youngest son develops a high fever and is admitted to a private clinic in Bangkok. The family has only basic insurance and no travel insurance. The clinic's invoice is much higher than the same care would cost in the Netherlands. How does the basic insurance reimburse this emergency care?", [["Up to the tariff customary for that care in the Netherlands", "Basic insurance generally covers care abroad up to the Dutch tariff; the excess is at the family's expense."], ["In full, regardless of the amount of the foreign invoice", "Full reimbursement of expensive foreign tariffs is not guaranteed under basic insurance."], ["Not at all, because basic insurance provides no cover outside Europe", "Basic insurance also reimburses care outside Europe, but up to the Dutch tariff level."], ["Only if they applied for an EHIC beforehand", "The EHIC works only within the EU, the EEA and Switzerland and is not a condition for reimbursement elsewhere."]], "1l.4"],
["Tom (29) lives with his girlfriend in Breda. He is going to work full-time as an employee at a logistics company in Antwerp. He works exclusively in Belgium and remains living in Breda. He asks his adviser whether he must keep his Dutch health insurance. What applies to his health insurance?", [["In principle he falls under the Belgian system, not the Zvw", "Under the European coordination rules the country-of-employment principle applies; with an S1 form Tom can also receive care in the Netherlands."], ["He remains subject to the insurance obligation in the Netherlands because he lives here", "When working as an employee in another EU country, the social security of the country of employment in principle applies."], ["He must have a full basic insurance in both Belgium and the Netherlands", "The European rules in fact prevent double insurance; only one country is competent."], ["He can choose for himself in which country he wants to be insured", "The applicable legislation follows from the coordination rules; there is no free choice."]], "1g.7"],
["Erik (44) is a fitter at a Dutch machine-building company and is married and the father of two children. His employer is posting him to a project in Germany for eighteen months. He has an A1 certificate and his family continues to live in the Netherlands. He wants to know whether he must take out health insurance in Germany. What does the A1 certificate mean for his health insurance?", [["He remains covered by Dutch social security and therefore by the Zvw", "With an A1 certificate for a posting, Dutch legislation continues to apply, including the insurance obligation."], ["He must cancel his Dutch health insurance and take out insurance in Germany", "With a posting under an A1 certificate, Erik in fact remains insured in the Netherlands."], ["He is not insured in any country during that period", "He remains insured under the Dutch rules."], ["He is insured in Germany only for emergency care", "His basic insurance continues in full."]], "1g.7"],
["Mrs De Groot (70) is a widow and moves to an apartment on the Costa Blanca in Spain. She receives only AOW (state pension) and a Dutch pension. Because she no longer lives in the Netherlands, she is no longer insured under the Wlz and her insurance obligation under the Zvw lapses. She has rheumatism and wants to stay in treatment in Spain. How does she arrange her care?", [["She registers via the CAK as a treaty beneficiary (verdragsgerechtigde) and pays a treaty contribution", "Treaty beneficiaries receive care in their country of residence at the expense of the Netherlands; the CAK arranges the registration and the contribution."], ["She keeps her ordinary Dutch basic insurance", "Without Wlz insurance she is no longer subject to the insurance obligation and cannot keep Zvw insurance."], ["She is automatically insured in Spain, without paying a contribution", "Because she has only a Dutch benefit, the Netherlands is responsible; for this she pays a contribution."], ["She registers with the Benefits Administration (Dienst Toeslagen) for a healthcare contribution", "The Benefits Administration implements allowances, not the registration of treaty beneficiaries."]], "1l.10"],
["When does a health insurer report a policyholder to the CAK under the defaulters scheme?", [["In the case of a premium arrear of six monthly premiums", "After six months of arrears the policyholder is reported to the CAK, which then starts levying an administrative-law premium (bestuursrechtelijke premie)."], ["At the first unpaid monthly premium", "Reminders and an offer of a payment arrangement come first."], ["Only after three years of premium arrears", "The scheme does not wait that long; it starts at an arrear of six monthly premiums."], ["Only if the insured person also does not pay his deductible", "It concerns arrears in the premium, not the deductible."]], "1a.2"],
["What does the administrative-law premium (bestuursrechtelijke premie) in the defaulters scheme involve?", [["A premium levied by the CAK, where possible at source", "The defaulter pays, instead of a premium to the insurer, a higher administrative-law premium, often through withholding at source."], ["A fine from the NZa for the health insurer", "The administrative-law premium is imposed on the insured person, not on the insurer."], ["A discount on the premium to repay the arrears faster", "It is in fact a higher premium, as an incentive to repay the debt."], ["A premium for a supplementary insurance that the CAK offers", "The CAK does not offer supplementary insurance."]], "1k.2"],
["What applies to a health insurer when a policyholder has a premium arrear of two monthly premiums?", [["The insurer must offer a payment arrangement", "The Zvw obliges the insurer to offer a payment arrangement at an arrear of two monthly premiums, to prevent further debts."], ["The insurer must terminate the basic insurance", "Termination is not the intention; the defaulters scheme in fact keeps the insured person insured."], ["The insurer must immediately report the insured person to the CAK", "Reporting to the CAK follows only at an arrear of six monthly premiums."], ["The insurer may no longer reimburse care", "The insured person retains the right to care under the basic insurance."]], "1a.2"],
["Dennis (31) is a bicycle courier in Amsterdam and returned to the Netherlands last year after a long trip. He has never taken out health insurance, because he is healthy and thinks the premium is too expensive. A data comparison shows that he is subject to the insurance obligation but not insured. He does not respond to the letters he receives about it. What may eventually follow?", [["After fines, the CAK may insure him ex officio with a health insurer", "The CAK tracks down uninsured people, imposes fines if there is no response and can ultimately insure someone ex officio."], ["He loses his right to health insurance for five years", "Exclusion is not possible; Dennis remains subject to the insurance obligation."], ["His client is obliged to take out health insurance for him", "The insurance obligation rests on Dennis himself."], ["The municipality automatically takes out a municipal group policy for him", "A municipal group policy is a voluntary group scheme, not a sanction for uninsured people."]], "1i.2"],
["What is the task of the National Health Care Institute?", [["Advising on the basic package and managing the Health Insurance Fund", "The National Health Care Institute advises the minister on the content of the package, manages the funds and carries out the risk equalisation."], ["Setting the premium of each health insurer", "Insurers set their own premium."], ["Exercising prudential supervision of health insurers", "Prudential supervision of health insurers lies with De Nederlandsche Bank."], ["Settling disputes between insured persons and insurers", "Disputes go to the SKGZ or the court."]], "1a.3"],
["What role does the Dutch Healthcare Authority (NZa) have with regard to health insurers?", [["Supervising the lawful implementation of the Zvw, such as the duty of care", "The NZa ensures that insurers implement the Zvw properly and sets rules for tariffs and performances in healthcare."], ["Determining the content of the basic package after advice from health insurers", "The package is determined by the government on the advice of the National Health Care Institute."], ["Assessing care under the Long-term Care Act", "Assessment for the Wlz is a task of the CIZ."], ["Collecting the income-related contribution under the Zvw", "That contribution is collected by the Tax Administration."]], "1a.3"],
["Which supervisor exercises prudential supervision of health insurers?", [["De Nederlandsche Bank", "As the prudential supervisor, DNB oversees the financial soundness of insurers, including health insurers."], ["The Health and Youth Care Inspectorate (IGJ)", "The IGJ supervises the quality and safety of care, not the solvency of insurers."], ["The Authority for Consumers and Markets (ACM)", "The ACM supervises competition, not the financial soundness of insurers."], ["The National Health Care Institute", "The National Health Care Institute is not a supervisor of the soundness of insurers."]], "1f.7"],
["An insured person disagrees with his health insurer's rejection of a claim. What is the correct order of steps?", [["First complain to the health insurer, then possibly go to the SKGZ", "The SKGZ deals with a complaint only once the insurer has first had the chance to resolve it itself."], ["Straight to Kifid", "Disputes about health insurance belong to the SKGZ, not to Kifid."], ["First a complaint to the NZa, then proceedings before the cantonal court", "The NZa does not handle individual disputes between insured person and insurer."], ["First to the National Health Care Institute, then to the health insurer itself", "The National Health Care Institute does not handle individual complaints from insured persons."]], "1a.9"],
["On which insurances can the SKGZ (Dutch Health Insurance Complaints and Disputes Foundation) give a ruling?", [["On both basic insurance and supplementary health insurance", "The SKGZ is the dispute resolution body for health insurance, both basic and supplementary."], ["Only on basic insurance", "The SKGZ can also handle complaints about supplementary health insurance."], ["Only on supplementary insurance", "Disputes about basic insurance also belong to the SKGZ."], ["On all non-life insurance, such as travel and contents insurance", "For other non-life insurance, Kifid is the complaints body."]], "1a.11"],
["A dispute at the SKGZ concerns the question of whether a treatment falls under the basic package. What role does the National Health Care Institute have in this?", [["The SKGZ asks the National Health Care Institute for advice", "In disputes about the content of the basic insurance, the disputes committee obtains advice from the National Health Care Institute."], ["The National Health Care Institute takes over the dispute and rules itself", "The National Health Care Institute only advises; the ruling is for the SKGZ."], ["The National Health Care Institute represents the health insurer", "The National Health Care Institute is independent and not a party to the dispute."], ["The National Health Care Institute plays no role in disputes about the package", "In disputes about the content of the package, its advice is in fact important."]], "1a.3"],
["What does a health insurer's duty of care under the Zvw involve?", [["Ensuring insured persons get the care they are entitled to, or its costs are reimbursed", "With benefits in kind, this means sufficient contracted care within a reasonable time and distance, with waiting-list mediation where necessary."], ["The insurer must personally advise each insured person annually on their health and lifestyle", "Health advice is not part of the insurer's duty of care."], ["The insurer must contract all care providers in the Netherlands at the same tariffs", "The insurer may contract selectively, as long as sufficient care is available."], ["The insurer must keep the premium the same every year", "The duty of care concerns the provision of care, not the level of the premium."]], "1i.3"],
["Henk (63) is a retired police officer and lives with his wife in Nijmegen. He asks his adviser for the cheapest basic insurance. Soon he will have a new knee at a hospital where he has been in treatment for years. He has great confidence in his orthopaedic surgeon there. What should the adviser in any case do?", [["Check whether the hospital is contracted and what otherwise is reimbursed", "With a benefits-in-kind or budget policy, non-contracted care may be reimbursed at a lower rate; for Henk that is essential information."], ["Only compare the premium, because the basic package is the same everywhere", "The package is the same, but the reimbursement of non-contracted care differs per policy."], ["Advise taking a voluntary deductible to save even more", "For a planned operation, a higher deductible is in fact unfavourable."], ["Refer Henk to the NZa for an overview of contracted hospitals per insurer", "The adviser must properly inform the client himself about the consequences of his choice."]], "2e.7"],
["What professional competence requirement applies under the Wft to an adviser who advises on health insurance?", [["He must hold the Wft Health Insurance diploma and keep his knowledge up to date through PE", "Advising on health insurance requires the specific Wft Health Insurance diploma; through permanent education the adviser remains professionally competent."], ["None, because basic insurance as statutory insurance is not a financial product within the meaning of the Wft", "Health insurance is non-life insurance and therefore a financial product under the Wft."], ["Only a medical qualification of at least higher professional education (hbo) level", "The Wft requires a Wft diploma, not a medical qualification."], ["Only the Wft Mortgage Credit diploma", "That diploma concerns mortgages, not health insurance."]], "1f.16"],
["What does the general duty of care of Article 4:24a Wft involve for a health insurance adviser?", [["He must carefully take the client's legitimate interests into account", "This open standard applies alongside the specific rules, for example when weighing policy type and deductible."], ["He must ensure that the client receives sufficient and timely care from his insurer", "That is the duty of care of the health insurer under the Zvw."], ["He must always advise the cheapest policy", "The client's interest is not always the lowest premium, for example where there is a need for free choice of doctor."], ["He must have the client switch every year", "Switching makes sense only if it is in the client's interest."]], "1f.16"],
["How is health data classified under the GDPR (AVG)?", [["As special category personal data; processing is prohibited unless a statutory exception applies", "Stricter rules apply to health data; processing is permitted only if an exception applies."], ["As ordinary personal data, like name and address, which may be freely processed with consent", "Health data fall into a stricter category than ordinary personal data."], ["As public data that may be freely shared", "Health data are in fact particularly sensitive and not freely shareable."], ["As data that only a doctor may view and a health insurer may never process", "Insurers may process health data under conditions, for example through a medical adviser."]], "1a.14"],
["A client completes a health declaration for a supplementary insurance and wants to hand it to his adviser. What is the careful way of working?", [["Have it sent directly or in a sealed envelope to the insurer's medical adviser", "In this way the health data remain limited to those who need them for the risk assessment."], ["Copy the declaration and keep it in the client file", "Unnecessarily retaining health data conflicts with data minimisation."], ["Assess the declaration himself and pass on only the outcome", "The adviser is not a medical adviser and should not assess the data."], ["Forward the declaration by ordinary email to the acceptance department so the application proceeds faster", "Sending unsecured to a general department does not fit the security requirements for special category data."]], "4a.3"],
["Within what period must a data breach that poses a risk to the persons concerned generally be reported to the Dutch Data Protection Authority?", [["Within 72 hours of discovery", "The GDPR requires a report within 72 hours after the organisation has discovered the breach, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk."], ["Within four weeks of discovery", "That period is too long; the GDPR requires a report within 72 hours."], ["Only in the annual accountability report", "A data breach must be reported immediately, not only afterwards in an annual report."], ["Within 24 hours to the AFM", "Data breaches are reported to the Dutch Data Protection Authority, not to the AFM."]], "1a.13"],
["Which GDPR principle means that an adviser does not process more personal data than is necessary for his advice?", [["Data minimisation", "Data minimisation means that only data that are necessary for the purpose are processed."], ["Data portability", "Data portability is the data subject's right to take his data with him."], ["Right to be forgotten", "That is the data subject's right to have data erased."], ["Privacy by design", "Privacy by design concerns building privacy into systems and processes, not specifically the extent of the processing."]], "1a.14"],
["Before engaging an adviser, a client wants to check whether that firm has a licence to advise on and mediate in health insurance. Which government source of information can he consult for this?", [["The AFM's public register", "The AFM maintains a public register of licensed financial service providers; consumers can search it themselves."], ["The register of the Dutch Healthcare Authority", "The NZa supervises care providers and health insurers, not the licensing of financial advisers."], ["The CAK's records", "The CAK collects, among other things, co-payments for the Wlz and Wmo and does not register advisers."], ["The rulings of the SKGZ", "The SKGZ handles complaints and disputes about health insurance, not advisers' licences."]], "1a.10"],
["What must an insurance distributor determine under the IDD before an insurance is concluded, even if he does not advise?", [["The client's demands and needs", "The IDD obliges distributors to determine the demands and needs and to offer only an insurance that matches them."], ["The complete asset position of all family members", "The IDD does not require such an extensive investigation."], ["Whether the client can also pay the premium in ten years", "That is not a specific IDD requirement for non-life insurance."], ["Whether the client has previously lodged a complaint with the SKGZ", "Previous complaints are not part of the demands-and-needs test."]], "1f.13"],
["An adviser receives an administrative fine from the AFM. He disagrees with it. Which route is open to him?", [["Objection, then appeal to the district court, then to the CBb", "Against an AFM decision an objection is first available; this is followed by an appeal to the district court (Rotterdam) and a further appeal to the Trade and Industry Appeals Tribunal (CBb)."], ["A complaint to Kifid, which can annul or mitigate the AFM's fine", "Kifid settles disputes between consumers and financial service providers, not sanctions imposed by the AFM."], ["Direct appeal to the Supreme Court, without first lodging an objection", "The Supreme Court is not the court for appeals against AFM decisions, and an objection must be lodged first."], ["Objection to De Nederlandsche Bank, as the highest financial supervisor", "DNB is not an appeal body for AFM decisions."]], "1a.12"],
["Kees (38) is a lorry driver and the father of a six-year-old son. He has been sentenced to eight months' imprisonment, which he is serving in a penitentiary institution. He has basic insurance with a large health insurer. His partner wonders whether she must keep paying his premium. What happens to Kees's health insurance during detention?", [["The insurance is suspended; the Ministry of Justice provides his care", "During lawful deprivation of liberty the health insurance is suspended, because the Ministry of Justice is then responsible for the detainee's care."], ["The insurance simply continues and the full premium remains due", "Kees would then be paying for care that the Ministry of Justice already provides; the Zvw in fact suspends the insurance."], ["The insurance ends permanently and he must apply for a new one after release", "The insurance does not end; after detention the cover revives without a new application."], ["He is automatically reported to the CAK as a defaulter", "The defaulters scheme concerns premium arrears, not detention."]], "1j.1"],
["An asylum seeker is staying in a COA (Central Agency for the Reception of Asylum Seekers) reception centre and his asylum procedure is still pending. How is his medical care arranged?", [["Through a separate scheme; he is not subject to the insurance obligation", "Asylum seekers in the procedure do not fall under the Zvw insurance obligation; their care is provided through a special scheme for asylum seekers."], ["He must take out basic insurance himself within four months", "Asylum seekers in the procedure are in fact not subject to the insurance obligation and do not have to take out basic insurance."], ["Through the municipality under the Social Support Act", "The Wmo concerns support for self-reliance for residents, not medical care for asylum seekers."], ["He is insured ex officio with a health insurer by the CAK", "Ex officio insurance is intended for people subject to the insurance obligation who do not take out insurance, and he is not one."]], "1i.2"],
["A care provider treats a patient who has no lawful residence in the Netherlands and cannot pay the bill. What applies?", [["He cannot insure himself; the provider can claim a contribution from the CAK", "Anyone without lawful residence is excluded from the Zvw; for medically necessary care the provider can claim a contribution through a CAK scheme."], ["The care provider's health insurer reimburses the treatment in full", "A care provider has no health insurance from which care to patients is paid; there is a separate scheme through the CAK."], ["The patient must be registered retroactively with a health insurer", "Without lawful residence the patient is not subject to the insurance obligation and cannot take out basic insurance."], ["The municipality must reimburse the costs through special assistance", "Special assistance is for residents with a right to social assistance; for this care there is a scheme through the CAK."]], "1a.3"],
["Marek (27) comes from Poland and works for seven months as an employee at a horticultural company in the Westland. He lives temporarily in housing arranged by his employer and pays wage tax here. His wife and daughter remain in Poland. He asks his employer whether his Polish insurance is sufficient. What applies to his health insurance?", [["He is subject to the insurance obligation here and must take out Dutch health insurance", "Anyone working in the Netherlands as an employee and paying wage tax here is insured under the Wlz and therefore subject to the Zvw insurance obligation, even for temporary work."], ["He remains insured exclusively in Poland, because he has Polish nationality", "Nationality is not decisive; within the EU the legislation of the country of employment in principle applies."], ["He becomes subject to the insurance obligation only if he works here for longer than twelve months", "No minimum period of work applies; the insurance obligation arises as soon as Marek works here as an employee."], ["He can choose whether to use the Dutch or the Polish insurance", "The insurance obligation is not a matter of choice; the applicable legislation follows from the European coordination rules."]], "1g.7"],
["Ingrid (40) lives with her husband and two children in Kleve, just across the border in Germany. She works exclusively in the Netherlands, as an employee physiotherapist at a hospital in Nijmegen. Her husband works in Germany and is insured there. Ingrid wants to know where she is insured and whether she can see a GP in Germany. What applies to her health insurance?", [["She is insured in the Netherlands and can also get care in Germany", "A cross-border worker falls under the legislation of the country of employment; under the European rules Ingrid can also receive care in her country of residence."], ["She is insured only in Germany, because she lives there", "When working as an employee in one country, the legislation of the country of employment in principle applies, not that of the country of residence."], ["She must take out a full basic insurance in both countries", "The European coordination rules in fact prevent double insurance; one set of legislation applies."], ["She is not subject to an insurance obligation anywhere and must take out private insurance", "Ingrid falls under the Dutch insurance obligation."]], "1g.7"],
["Sanne (21) studies law in Leiden and is going to study in Madrid for a year on an exchange. She remains a resident of the Netherlands and is registered at her parents' address in Leiderdorp. She has a mild form of epilepsy and takes medication daily. She wonders whether she may keep her Dutch health insurance. What applies to her health insurance?", [["She remains subject to the insurance obligation and keeps her Dutch health insurance", "As long as Sanne remains a resident of the Netherlands, she remains insured under the Wlz and subject to the insurance obligation; in Spain she can use her EHIC."], ["She must cancel her health insurance as soon as she is away for more than three months", "The duration of the stay is not decisive; what matters is whether she remains a resident of the Netherlands."], ["She must take compulsory insurance in the Spanish system", "A temporary study stay does not make her subject to the insurance obligation in Spain as long as she remains a resident here."], ["During her studies she is covered only through a supplementary insurance", "A supplementary insurance does not replace the basic insurance; that remains mandatory."]], "1g.7"],
["When does health insurance end if the insured person dies?", [["By operation of law, with effect from the day after the death", "The Zvw provides that health insurance ends automatically after death; the surviving relatives do not need to cancel it."], ["Only when the surviving relatives cancel the insurance in writing", "Cancellation is not needed; the insurance ends by operation of law."], ["On 1 January of the year after the death", "The insurance does not continue until the end of the year, because the insurance obligation lapses on death."], ["After the notary has issued the certificate of inheritance", "The end of the insurance does not depend on the settlement of the estate."]], "1k.1"],
["Parents take out health insurance for their 9-year-old daughter. Who is the policyholder and who is the insured person?", [["The parent is the policyholder, the child is the insured person", "The policyholder concludes the contract and is the point of contact; the insured person is the one entitled to care, here the child."], ["The child is both policyholder and insured person", "A 9-year-old child does not conclude the contract herself; the parent does so as policyholder."], ["The health insurer is the policyholder, the parent is the insured person", "The insurer is the counterparty that bears the risk, not the policyholder."], ["The parent is the insured person and the child is the beneficiary of the policy", "The concept of beneficiary belongs to life insurance; in health insurance the child herself is the insured person."]], "1i.9"],
["Lotte lives with her parents in Assen and is following a vocational (mbo) course to become a doctor's assistant. She turns 18 on 12 March. She has agreed with her parents that she will then pay her health premium herself from her part-time job. She wants to know from what moment she must pay. From when is premium for basic insurance due for Lotte?", [["From 1 April, the month after her birthday", "Insured persons under 18 pay no premium; the premium obligation begins on the first day of the month after the 18th birthday."], ["From 12 March, the day of her birthday", "The premium obligation does not begin on the birthday itself, but on the first day of the following month."], ["From 1 January of the year in which she turns 18", "No premium is due for the months in which Lotte was still a minor."], ["From 1 January of the year after she turned 18", "She would then be insured free of charge for months as an adult; the premium obligation begins earlier."]], "1i.2"],
["Which body determines, in cases of doubt, whether someone is insured under the Long-term Care Act, and thereby subject to the Zvw insurance obligation?", [["The Social Insurance Bank (SVB)", "The SVB decides on the insurance position for the national insurance schemes, including the Wlz; the Zvw insurance obligation follows from that."], ["The Dutch Healthcare Authority (NZa)", "The NZa supervises health insurers and healthcare markets, but does not decide on anyone's insurance position."], ["The Care Needs Assessment Centre (CIZ)", "The CIZ assesses whether someone is entitled to Wlz care, not whether someone is insured under the Wlz."], ["The health insurer with which the person registers", "The health insurer implements the insurance, but does not determine the insurance position for the national insurance schemes."]], "1i.2"],
["What has applied since 2023 regarding group discounts on the premium of basic insurance?", [["That discount has been abolished; benefits now exist only in supplementary insurance", "Since 2023 no group discount may be given on basic insurance; discounts on supplementary insurance remain possible."], ["The maximum discount has been raised to make group schemes more attractive", "The discount has not been raised but abolished, because it contributed little to better care procurement."], ["Only employer group schemes may still give a discount on basic insurance", "The ban applies to all group schemes, including those of employers."], ["The discount has become mandatory for all municipal group health insurance schemes", "Municipal group policies also no longer give a discount on basic insurance; they differentiate themselves through supplementary cover."]], "1b.3"],
["Which rule applies to the profit of a health insurer that carries out basic insurance?", [["The health insurer may not distribute profit as dividend to shareholders", "A dividend ban applies to health insurers; a positive result stays in the company, for example for reserves or premium smoothing."], ["Profit must be paid over in full to the Health Insurance Fund", "There is no obligation to pay profit over to the fund; the fund is fed by premiums and contributions."], ["Profit may be freely distributed once solvency is sufficient", "Even with sufficient solvency, distributing profit to shareholders remains prohibited."], ["Profit must be returned to insured persons every year in the form of a premium discount", "There is no statutory obligation to return profit annually as a discount; the insurer may hold reserves."]], "1a.1"],
["Within what period must a health insurer at the very least announce a premium increase effective 1 January to its policyholders?", [["At least six weeks before the change takes effect", "The Zvw obliges the insurer to notify a change to the policyholder's disadvantage at least six weeks in advance, so that the policyholder can compare and switch in good time."], ["By 31 December at the latest, the last day for cancelling", "That is too late; the policyholder would then have no time to compare."], ["Only in January, with the first premium collection", "Notifying afterwards is not permitted; the policyholder must be able to decide in advance."], ["At least three months before the change takes effect", "A three-month period does not apply; the statutory period is shorter."]], "1k.8"],
["A health insurer changes the policy conditions mid-year to the disadvantage of insured persons. What can the policyholder do?", [["Cancel as of the date the change takes effect", "In the case of a change to his disadvantage, the policyholder has a special right of cancellation and can switch with effect from the date the change takes effect."], ["Nothing; switching is possible only on 1 January", "In addition to the annual switching option, a special right of cancellation exists in the case of a disadvantageous change."], ["Have the change annulled by the Dutch Healthcare Authority", "The NZa does not annul individual policy conditions; the insured person can, however, cancel."], ["Cancel only the supplementary insurance, not the basic insurance", "The right of cancellation in the case of a disadvantageous change in fact also applies to the basic insurance."]], "1k.8"],
["Thomas (34) is under guardianship (curatele). His health insurance needs to be adjusted. Who acts on Thomas's behalf when concluding or changing his health insurance?", [["His guardian (curator), as Thomas is legally incapable of acting", "Anyone under guardianship cannot perform legal acts independently; the guardian represents him."], ["Thomas himself, because guardianship concerns only his income", "Guardianship is the most far-reaching protective measure and applies to both personal and financial matters."], ["His health insurer, which adjusts the policy ex officio", "A health insurer does not act on behalf of the insured person; the statutory representative does."], ["The cantonal court judge, who decides separately on every change to the policy", "The cantonal court judge establishes the guardianship and appoints the guardian, but does not arrange the policy himself."]], "1b.1"],
["Does a second opinion from another specialist about one's own treatment fall under basic insurance?", [["Yes, it falls under basic insurance, under the ordinary conditions such as a referral", "Basic insurance reimburses a second opinion that relates to one's own treatment, provided the normal conditions such as a referral have been met."], ["A second opinion is reimbursed only from supplementary insurance", "A second opinion belongs to medical specialist care in basic insurance."], ["A second opinion is possible only with the first specialist's permission", "The first practitioner's permission is not a condition; the insured person has a right to a second opinion himself."], ["A second opinion falls under the Wmo and must always be applied for from the municipality", "The Wmo concerns social support, not medical assessments by specialists."]], "1d.1"],
["Bas (30) works as a programmer in Den Bosch and lives with his boyfriend. Since a reorganisation has been looming at work, he has been feeling low and sleeping badly. His GP refers him for a few sessions to the practice support worker for mental healthcare (POH-GGZ) in the GP practice. Bas has not yet used any care this year. How are these sessions reimbursed?", [["As GP care from basic insurance, without a deductible", "The POH-GGZ works within the GP practice; this care falls under GP care, to which no deductible applies."], ["From basic insurance, with the mandatory deductible applying", "That applies to basic and specialised mental healthcare, not to sessions with the POH-GGZ in the GP practice."], ["Only from supplementary insurance", "This care belongs to GP care in basic insurance."], ["Through the municipality, under the Youth Act", "The Youth Act applies to young people under 18; Bas is 30."]], "1g.2"],
["Do laboratory tests, such as blood tests requested by the GP, count towards the mandatory deductible?", [["Yes, laboratory tests fall under the deductible, even if the GP requests them", "Only care provided by the GP himself is exempted; laboratory testing is a separate service that does fall under the deductible."], ["No, everything the GP requests falls outside the deductible", "The exception applies to GP care itself, not to medicines or tests that the GP requests."], ["No, laboratory tests fall entirely outside basic insurance", "Laboratory tests requested by the GP are reimbursed from basic insurance."], ["Only if the test is carried out in a hospital laboratory rather than at the GP", "Whether the deductible applies does not depend on the location of the laboratory."]], "1g.2"],
["What applies in basic insurance to the costs of maternity care after a home birth?", [["A co-payment per hour applies, but no deductible", "Maternity care falls outside the deductible in basic insurance; the insured person does pay a statutory co-payment per hour."], ["Maternity care is charged in full to the mandatory deductible", "Maternity care is in fact exempted from the deductible."], ["Maternity care does not fall under basic insurance and must be insured as a supplement", "Maternity care is in basic insurance; supplementary insurance can reimburse the co-payment, however."], ["Maternity care is arranged and paid for through the municipality's Wmo", "Maternity care is Zvw care, not a municipal service."]], "1d.8"],
["Femke (30) is pregnant with her first child and works as a teacher at a primary school in Alkmaar. The pregnancy is progressing without complications, and the midwife sees no medical reason for a hospital birth. Femke nevertheless feels safer in hospital and wants to give birth there as an outpatient. She has only basic insurance. What applies to the reimbursement?", [["The birth is reimbursed, but she pays a co-payment", "For an outpatient hospital birth without a medical indication a statutory co-payment applies; with a medical indication it does not."], ["A hospital birth without a medical indication is not reimbursed", "The birth itself is reimbursed; a co-payment applies for the use of the hospital facilities."], ["A hospital birth is always reimbursed in full", "Without a medical indication a co-payment applies."], ["She must first ask permission from the National Health Care Institute", "The National Health Care Institute does not decide on individual reimbursements; the health insurer does so under the policy."]], "1d.8"],
["For whom is seated patient transport, such as by taxi or own car, reimbursed from basic insurance?", [["Only for certain groups, such as patients undergoing kidney dialysis or chemotherapy", "Seated patient transport is limited to fixed groups, such as dialysis and oncology patients, the visually impaired and wheelchair users, with a hardship clause."], ["For every insured person who has to travel to a hospital or specialist for an appointment", "Seated patient transport is not intended for everyone; basic insurance reimburses it only for specific groups."], ["Only for insured persons aged 65 and over without their own transport", "Age is not a criterion; what matters is the nature of the treatment or impairment."], ["For no one; transport always falls under the municipality's Wmo", "Ambulance transport and seated patient transport for certain groups do fall under the Zvw."]], "1l.1"],
["Which of the following schemes is an employee insurance?", [["The Sickness Benefits Act (Ziektewet)", "The Ziektewet is an employee insurance that covers loss of wages through illness, including for employees without an employer who continues to pay wages."], ["The General Old Age Pensions Act (AOW)", "The AOW is a national insurance for residents, not only for employees."], ["The Long-term Care Act", "The Wlz is a national insurance, not limited to employees."], ["The General Surviving Dependants Act", "The Anw is a national insurance for surviving dependants."]], "1c.2"],
["How much dietary advice from a dietitian does basic insurance reimburse per calendar year?", [["A maximum of three treatment hours", "Basic insurance reimburses dietary advice with a medical purpose up to three treatment hours per calendar year; more may be insured as a supplement."], ["Unlimited, as long as the GP refers", "A referral does not make the reimbursement unlimited; a maximum number of hours applies."], ["Nothing; dietetics is only in supplementary insurance", "Dietetics is in basic insurance, albeit to a limited extent."], ["A maximum of ten treatment hours, as with occupational therapy", "Ten treatment hours applies to occupational therapy, not to dietetics."]], "1l.1"],
["What applies to insurance premium tax on the premium of a supplementary health insurance?", [["Health insurance is exempt from insurance premium tax", "The Legal Transactions Taxation Act exempts health insurance; the premium therefore consists of risk premium, costs and profit margin, without this tax."], ["The general rate of insurance premium tax is due on the premium", "That rate applies to many non-life insurances, but health insurance is exempt."], ["Insurance premium tax is due only above a certain annual premium", "No premium threshold applies; health insurance is exempt entirely."], ["The insured person can reclaim the insurance premium tax through the healthcare allowance", "The healthcare allowance is a contribution towards the premium and has nothing to do with insurance premium tax."]], "1c.6"],
["What applies to IVF in basic insurance?", [["A maximum of three attempts per pregnancy to be achieved, for women under 43", "Basic insurance reimburses IVF up to three attempts per pregnancy to be achieved and only for women under 43."], ["An unlimited number of attempts, regardless of the woman's age", "The number of attempts and the age are in fact limited."], ["IVF falls outside basic insurance and can only be insured as a supplement", "IVF is part of basic insurance, under conditions."], ["A maximum of one attempt, only with a medical referral from the GP", "Basic insurance reimburses more than one attempt."]], "1l.1"],
["What applies in basic insurance to a stop-smoking programme?", [["It is reimbursed and does not fall under the deductible", "A stop-smoking programme is in basic insurance and exempted from the deductible, to keep the threshold low."], ["It falls under basic insurance, but the deductible applies in full", "Precisely in order to discourage smoking, this programme is exempted from the deductible."], ["It is reimbursed only from supplementary insurance", "The programme is in the basic package."], ["The municipality reimburses it through the Wmo as a preventive service", "The programme falls under the Zvw, not the Wmo."]], "1g.2"],
["Mr Bos (54) is a bus driver in Tilburg, married and the father of two adult children. He is severely overweight and has high blood pressure, and therefore an increased risk of cardiovascular disease. His GP refers him to a combined lifestyle intervention (GLI). He is afraid this programme will cost a lot of money. What is correct about the reimbursement of the GLI?", [["The GLI is in basic insurance and does not fall under the deductible", "The GLI focuses on nutrition, exercise and behaviour and is exempted from the deductible."], ["The GLI is a sports membership that the municipality reimburses", "The GLI is a programme guided by a lifestyle coach and falls under the Zvw."], ["The GLI falls under basic insurance, with a co-payment of half", "No such co-payment applies to the GLI, and the deductible does not apply."], ["The GLI is reimbursed only from supplementary insurance", "The GLI belongs to the basic package."]], "1g.2"],
["Does an aid that an insured person receives on loan, such as a wheelchair for short-term use through the health insurer, count towards the deductible?", [["No, aids on loan are exempted from the deductible", "For aids provided on loan the deductible does not apply; the insured person does not become the owner."], ["Yes, all aids count in full towards the deductible", "In fact an exception applies to aids on loan."], ["Only if the aid is used for longer than a year", "The duration of use is not decisive; what matters is provision on loan."], ["No, because aids are never reimbursed from basic insurance, only through the Wmo", "Aids are in the basic package."]], "1g.2"],
["What applies to the reimbursement of a hearing aid for an adult insured person?", [["The hearing aid falls under basic insurance, with a co-payment for adults", "Hearing aids are aids in the basic package; insured persons aged 18 and over pay a statutory co-payment."], ["Hearing aids are reimbursed only to children under 18", "Adults are also entitled to a hearing aid from basic insurance."], ["A hearing aid falls under the Wmo and must be applied for from the municipality as a service", "Hearing aids are aids under the Zvw, not the Wmo."], ["A hearing aid is reimbursed only from supplementary insurance", "The hearing aid is in basic insurance."]], "1d.8"],
["Are glasses for an adult reimbursed from basic insurance?", [["As a rule not, except for certain medical indications", "Glasses and lenses for adults in principle fall outside the basic package; reimbursement exists only for specific medical indications."], ["Yes, every adult is entitled to glasses once every two years", "A periodic right to glasses does not exist in basic insurance."], ["Yes, but only if the optician is contracted", "Contracting does not change the fact that glasses in principle fall outside the package."], ["No, glasses are provided exclusively by the municipality through the Wmo", "Glasses are not a Wmo service; they can be insured as a supplement, however."]], "1l.1"],
["Mrs Hoek (55) is a receptionist at a hotel in Maastricht. She feels that her upper eyelids have looked heavy and tired in recent years. An ophthalmologist has established that her field of vision is not restricted. She nevertheless wants to have the eyelids corrected by a plastic surgeon. Is this procedure reimbursed from basic insurance?", [["No, a purely cosmetic procedure falls outside basic insurance", "Plastic surgery is reimbursed only in the case of, for example, a demonstrable functional disorder; without a restriction of the field of vision there is none."], ["Yes, all procedures by a plastic surgeon fall in basic insurance", "The basic package reimburses plastic surgery only for certain medical reasons."], ["Yes, provided she first chooses a higher voluntary deductible", "The amount of the deductible does not determine what falls in the package."], ["Yes, if she is treated in a contracted hospital", "Contracting does not change the content of the package."]], "1l.1"],
["Joyce goes to a medical specialist without a referral from a GP. What can the consequence be for reimbursement from basic insurance?", [["Reimbursement can be refused, because a referral is generally required", "The policy makes a referral by, for example, the GP a condition for reimbursement of medical specialist care."], ["No consequence; a referral is needed only with a reimbursement policy", "The referral requirement applies to both benefits-in-kind and reimbursement policies."], ["The care is then automatically reimbursed from the supplementary insurance", "A supplementary insurance does not take over the referral requirement of the basic insurance."], ["She must recover the costs from the specialist, because he was not allowed to treat her", "The specialist may treat her; the only question is whether the health insurer reimburses."]], "1l.1"],
["What does the medicines reimbursement system (GVS) involve?", [["A limit applies per group of comparable medicines; above it a co-payment is paid", "The GVS divides comparable medicines into groups; if a medicine is more expensive than the limit, the insured person pays the difference as a co-payment, up to a statutory maximum."], ["Each health insurer determines entirely on its own which medicines are in the basic package", "Which medicines are in the package is determined by the minister; within that framework the insurer chooses through preferential policy."], ["All medicines are reimbursed in full once the deductible has been paid", "Even after the deductible, a co-payment may apply for a medicine above the reimbursement limit."], ["Medicines are reimbursed only if the pharmacy prepares them itself", "The GVS concerns registered medicines, not pharmacy preparations."]], "1d.8"],
["What does it mean that a health insurer requires prior authorisation for certain care?", [["The insured person must have the insurer's permission in advance in order to be reimbursed", "For care subject to authorisation, the insurer checks in advance whether the insured person needs that care; without authorisation, reimbursement can be refused."], ["The care provider must have a licence from the NZa for that care", "An authorisation concerns the insurer's permission for the insured person, not a licence for the provider."], ["The insured person must give his GP a power of attorney to submit claims", "An authorisation in the policy is not a power of attorney for the GP."], ["The care is reimbursed only after the National Health Care Institute has issued advice on that treatment", "The National Health Care Institute advises on the package in general, not on individual applications."]], "1l.7"],
["What does it mean that the basic package of the Zvw is described in a function-oriented way?", [["The law says which care is insured, not who must provide it", "A function-oriented description lays down which care is insured; which provider delivers that care may be worked out by the insurer in the policy."], ["Only care that restores bodily functions falls under the basic package", "Function-oriented refers to the way of describing, not to a restriction to restoring bodily functions."], ["The insured person decides for himself which treatment he needs", "Whether someone needs care is determined on the basis of the state of science and practice."], ["Each health insurer may determine the content of the package itself", "The content of the package is laid down by law; only the implementation may differ per policy."]], "1d.1"],
["Who determines the assessment for district nursing under the Zvw?", [["The district nurse", "The assessment for nursing and care at home is made by a qualified district nurse, not by the CIZ or the municipality."], ["The Care Needs Assessment Centre (CIZ)", "The CIZ assesses for the Wlz, not for district nursing under the Zvw."], ["The municipality, after a kitchen table conversation", "The kitchen table conversation belongs to the Wmo; district nursing falls under the Zvw."], ["The health insurer through a medical adviser", "The insurer may check, but the assessment itself is made by the district nurse."]], "1i.1"],
["Lars (24) studies architecture in Delft and lives in a student house. On Saturday evening he cuts his hand deeply while cooking. He first goes to the out-of-hours GP service and is then sent on to the hospital's emergency department (SEH), where the wound is stitched. He has not yet used any care this year. Which care counts towards his deductible?", [["Only the care at the emergency department", "Care at the out-of-hours GP service is GP care and falls outside the deductible; care at the emergency department is hospital care and does count."], ["Both the out-of-hours GP service and the emergency department", "GP care, including outside office hours at the out-of-hours GP service, is exempted from the deductible."], ["Neither, because it concerns emergency care at the weekend", "There is no general exception for emergency care or weekend care."], ["Only the out-of-hours GP service, because he went there without a referral", "It is the other way round: the out-of-hours GP service falls outside the deductible, the emergency department does not."]], "1g.2"],
["What applies to mental healthcare (GGZ) by a psychologist or psychiatrist for an insured person aged 25?", [["It falls under basic insurance, with a referral and deductible", "For adults, mental healthcare is in basic insurance; as a rule a referral is needed and the mandatory deductible applies."], ["It falls under the Youth Act until the insured person is 27", "The Youth Act in principle applies up to age 18; for adults mental healthcare falls under the Zvw."], ["It is reimbursed only from supplementary insurance", "Mental healthcare for adults belongs to the basic package."], ["It falls under basic insurance and is exempted from the deductible", "Unlike the POH-GGZ in the GP practice, this mental healthcare does fall under the deductible."]], "1i.1"],
["To which care is an insured person entitled under the Zvw, in addition to the condition that the care meets the state of science and practice?", [["To care he reasonably needs in content and scope", "The criterion of 'reasonably required' limits the entitlement: the insured person receives the care he needs given his situation, no more."], ["To all care that his practitioner considers desirable", "The practitioner's wish is not decisive; the care must fit what the insured person reasonably needs."], ["To all care for which he is willing to pay the deductible", "Paying the deductible does not give a right to care outside the package."], ["To care that in the first place has the lowest cost", "The criterion is not the lowest price, but whether the insured person needs the care."]], "1i.2"],
["Can an insured person cover the mandatory deductible with a supplementary insurance?", [["No, the mandatory deductible may not be insured", "The insured person must bear the deductible himself to encourage cost awareness; an insurance that covers it is not permitted."], ["Yes, every supplementary insurance automatically covers the deductible", "Supplementary insurances may in fact not reimburse the mandatory deductible."], ["Yes, but only through an employer group scheme", "Covering the deductible is not permitted through a group scheme either."], ["Only for insured persons with a chronic condition", "For chronically ill people there is no exception to the ban on insuring the deductible."]], "1d.8"],
["A health insurer waives the deductible if an insured person uses a certain medicine or goes to a designated care provider. Is that permitted?", [["Yes, the insurer may then waive the deductible in whole or in part", "The Zvw permits the insurer not to apply the deductible when designated providers or medicines are used, to encourage efficient choices."], ["No, the deductible must be applied to the same care for every insured person", "The law in fact gives insurers room not to apply the deductible in these cases."], ["Only with the prior consent of each individual insured person", "It concerns a policy arrangement; individual consent is not the criterion."], ["Only if the NZa grants an exemption for each care provider", "No exemption per care provider is needed; it is a choice within the policy."]], "1d.8"],
["What option must a health insurer offer insured persons, under conditions, when paying the mandatory deductible?", [["Paying the mandatory deductible spread over instalments", "Health insurers must offer insured persons, under conditions, the option of paying the mandatory deductible in instalments."], ["Having the deductible waived in the case of a low income", "There is no statutory exemption from the deductible on grounds of income; a municipal group policy can compensate, however."], ["Having the deductible offset against next year's healthcare allowance", "The healthcare allowance and the deductible are not offset against each other by the insurer."], ["Postponing the deductible until he retires", "Postponement until retirement is not a scheme that insurers offer or must offer."]], "1c.9"],
["Naomi (28) is a shop assistant in a clothing store and lives alone in Utrecht. To save premium she has chosen a voluntary deductible. This year she suffers from recurring bladder infections and goes to the GP a few times. She is afraid that every visit will be deducted from her deductible. What applies to these GP visits?", [["The voluntary deductible does not apply to GP care either", "The voluntary deductible applies to the same care as the mandatory deductible; GP care is exempted from it."], ["The GP visits do fall under her voluntary deductible", "The voluntary deductible has the same exceptions as the mandatory one, so also for the GP."], ["She pays for the visits herself and then claims them from the municipality", "The municipality does not reimburse GP care; it falls under basic insurance."], ["With a voluntary deductible the right to GP care lapses", "A voluntary deductible does not restrict the cover; it only increases the amount she bears herself."]], "1d.8"],
["When can an insured person change the amount of his voluntary deductible?", [["As a rule only on 1 January, for a new calendar year", "The voluntary deductible is chosen per calendar year; reducing it mid-year when care turns out to be needed is generally not possible."], ["At any time, even immediately before a planned treatment", "The insured person would then reduce the deductible only when he needs care; therefore this is possible only per new year."], ["Only on moving to another municipality", "A move does not give a right to change the voluntary deductible mid-year."], ["Once every five years, with the insurer's permission", "There is no five-year period; the choice can be made annually."]], "3d.1"],
["How does the mandatory deductible apply to two partners who are on one policy with the same insurer?", [["Per insured person aged 18 or over separately, per calendar year", "The deductible is personal: every adult insured person has their own deductible, even if they are on one policy."], ["One joint deductible for the whole household", "There is no household deductible; it applies per insured person."], ["Only for the policyholder, not for the co-insured partner", "The co-insured partner aged 18 or over also has a deductible."], ["Per treatment, regardless of how much care is used in a year", "The deductible applies per calendar year, not per treatment."]], "1d.8"],
["Jan (47) is a software architect and emigrates permanently to Canada with his wife and son on 1 July. His insurance obligation and his Dutch health insurance thereby end. In the first half of the year he was treated in hospital for a broken wrist. He wants to know how much deductible he pays for that year. How high is his mandatory deductible for the year of emigration?", [["Pro rata to the period in which he was insured", "If the insurance does not run for the whole calendar year, the deductible applies in proportion to the insured period."], ["The full amount, because the deductible applies per calendar year", "For an insurance that runs for part of the year, the deductible is calculated pro rata."], ["Zero, because the deductible lapses on emigration", "For the months that Jan was insured, a deductible continues to apply."], ["Double the amount, as a penalty for the mid-year termination", "Such a penalty does not exist."]], "1j.2"],
["Monique (49) is an office manager in Zoetermeer and has a benefits-in-kind policy. She has her gall bladder removed in a contracted hospital. She has not yet used her deductible this year. After the operation she wonders whether an invoice will come from the hospital. How does payment generally proceed?", [["The hospital bills the insurer; the insurer charges the deductible to Monique", "With contracted benefits-in-kind care, the care provider settles directly with the insurer; Monique receives only a bill for the deductible."], ["Monique pays the invoice herself and then claims it from the insurer", "Advancing payment and claiming is characteristic of care outside the contract or of a reimbursement policy."], ["The hospital sends the bill to the CAK, which collects the amount from her", "The CAK collects co-payments for the Wlz and Wmo, not for hospital care under the Zvw."], ["The municipality pays the hospital and offsets it against municipal taxes", "Hospital care falls under the Zvw and is not paid through the municipality."]], "1l.13"],
["Tim (37) has multiple sclerosis and receives physiotherapy that falls under his basic insurance. He has a reimbursement policy. After moving to Zwolle he chooses a physiotherapist who has no contract with his insurer. He wonders what that means for payment. What can happen to Tim in this situation?", [["He may have to pay the invoice himself first and then claim it from his insurer", "With reimbursement Tim is free in his choice, but a non-contracted provider may send the invoice to him, which he then claims."], ["He receives nothing reimbursed, because the physiotherapist has no contract", "A reimbursement policy in fact also reimburses care from non-contracted providers, up to the market-conform tariff."], ["He must first ask permission from the National Health Care Institute", "The National Health Care Institute does not decide on individual reimbursements."], ["He must switch to a benefits-in-kind policy in order to be allowed to claim", "Claiming in fact belongs to the reimbursement policy."]], "1l.13"],
["Mrs Lammers (64) is a teacher and lives with her husband in Gouda. She has had supplementary insurance for years, but hardly uses it. From 1 January she wants to cancel only her supplementary insurance and keep her basic insurance with the same insurer. She asks her adviser whether that can be done separately. Can Mrs Lammers arrange it that way?", [["Yes, that is possible; the basic insurance simply continues", "Basic and supplementary insurance are separate contracts; cancelling the supplementary insurance leaves the basic insurance untouched."], ["No, basic and supplementary insurance can only be cancelled together", "The link works at most the other way round: some insurers offer supplementary insurance only alongside their own basic insurance."], ["Yes, but then her right to the healthcare allowance also lapses", "The right to the healthcare allowance depends on the basic insurance, not on the supplementary insurance."], ["No, a supplementary insurance can be cancelled only after five years", "No such minimum term of five years applies."]], "1k.8"],
["What may an insured person expect under the duty of care of his health insurer if the waiting time for an operation is well above the acceptable standard?", [["Help with care mediation to a provider with a shorter waiting time", "The duty of care means that the insurer ensures timely care; in the case of long waiting times he must mediate towards a suitable alternative."], ["Nothing; waiting times are solely the hospital's responsibility", "It is precisely the health insurer who, through its duty of care, is responsible for timely access to care."], ["Compensation for each week of waiting time above the standard", "A fixed compensation per week of waiting time is not part of the duty of care."], ["A reduction of his premium until the operation has taken place", "The duty of care does not lead to a premium reduction; the insurer must ensure that care is available in good time."]], "1i.4"],
["Which legislation applies to a supplementary health insurance?", [["The insurance law of the Dutch Civil Code (BW) and the Wft, not the Zvw", "A supplementary insurance is an ordinary private non-life insurance; rules such as the obligation to accept applicants and the ban on premium differentiation of the Zvw do not apply to it."], ["Exclusively the Health Insurance Act, as with basic insurance", "The Zvw regulates only basic insurance; supplementary insurances fall outside it."], ["The Long-term Care Act, because it concerns extra care", "The Wlz is a national insurance for long-term care and does not regulate supplementary insurances."], ["The Wmo 2015, because municipalities determine the supplementary packages", "Municipalities do not determine supplementary packages; those are a product of the insurer."]], "1a.6"],
["Gerard (50) is an installation engineer in Hengelo and has suffered for years from a herniated disc in his lower back. He applies for extensive supplementary insurance with a lot of physiotherapy. On the health declaration he does not mention his back complaints, because he is afraid of otherwise being refused. A year later he submits a large claim for back treatments. What can be the consequence of the non-disclosure?", [["The insurer can invoke breach of the duty of disclosure", "For supplementary insurance, the pre-contractual duty of disclosure under the BW applies; non-disclosure can lead to refusal of the benefit or cancellation."], ["No consequence, because the obligation to accept applicants also applies to supplementary insurance", "The obligation to accept applicants applies only to basic insurance."], ["His basic insurance is terminated retroactively", "The duty of disclosure for the supplementary insurance has no consequences for the basic insurance."], ["The SKGZ imposes an administrative fine on him for the non-disclosure", "The SKGZ settles disputes and does not impose fines."]], "1a.4"],
["Ricardo (35) is a cook in a restaurant in Rotterdam and has money worries because of a divorce. He has basic insurance and supplementary insurance with dental cover with the same insurer. He now has a premium arrear of three months. His insurer sends him a reminder. What may the insurer do with his supplementary insurance that it may not do with the basic insurance?", [["Suspend the cover or terminate the insurance", "With a supplementary insurance the insurer may, in the event of non-payment, suspend the cover or cancel; with basic insurance the defaulters scheme applies and the cover remains in place."], ["Retroactively double the premium", "A retroactive doubling of the premium is not permitted."], ["Immediately report him to the CAK for an administrative-law premium", "The CAK scheme belongs to basic insurance and follows only at an arrear of six monthly premiums."], ["Have his healthcare allowance withheld by the Benefits Administration", "The Benefits Administration does not withhold healthcare allowance for arrears on supplementary insurance."]], "1a.2"],
["What is a typical feature of a supplementary dental insurance?", [["A maximum reimbursement per calendar year and sometimes a percentage of the costs", "Supplementary dental insurances generally reimburse up to a maximum amount per year, often for a percentage of the invoice."], ["A statutorily determined cover that is the same at all insurers", "The content of supplementary insurances is not laid down by law and differs per insurer."], ["Full reimbursement of all dental costs without a maximum", "Unlimited reimbursement is unusual; insurers apply maxima."], ["An obligation to accept all applicants without questions about the condition of their teeth", "No obligation to accept applicants applies to supplementary insurance; insurers can ask about the condition of the teeth."]], "1d.4"],
["May a health insurer still give a discount on a supplementary insurance through a group scheme?", [["Yes, discounts on supplementary insurances are permitted", "The ban on group discounts applies only to basic insurance; for supplementary insurances a group scheme may offer a discount or extra cover."], ["No, since 2023 every group discount has been prohibited", "The abolition in 2023 applied only to basic insurance."], ["Only if the discount is also given to non-members", "A group discount is in fact reserved for participants in the group scheme."], ["Only for municipal policies for people on a low income", "Other group schemes, such as those of employers, may also give a discount on supplementary insurances."]], "1b.3"],
["The Kok family, two parents and two teenagers from Hoorn, are on holiday in Italy. Father is injured in a car accident and treated in an Italian hospital. As soon as he can be moved, the family wants to have him transported to the Netherlands by air ambulance. They have basic insurance and a continuous travel insurance. From what can that return transport be reimbursed?", [["From the travel insurance or a suitable supplementary insurance", "Repatriation is not part of the basic package; a travel insurance or a supplementary insurance with this cover is needed for it."], ["From basic insurance, because it concerns medically necessary care", "Basic insurance reimburses emergency care on the spot, but not repatriation to the Netherlands."], ["From the European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)", "The EHIC entitles the holder to medically necessary care in the country of stay, not to return transport."], ["From the Wmo of the municipality of residence, because it concerns transport", "The Wmo regulates transport services in one's own municipality, not repatriation from abroad."]], "1l.11"],
["Marieke (34) works as a dental assistant and has a chronic neck complaint. This condition is not on the list of chronic conditions for physiotherapy in basic insurance. She goes to the physiotherapist about twenty times a year and now pays for it herself. She wants to adjust her insurance from 1 January so that she pays less herself. What is suitable advice?", [["A supplementary insurance with sufficient physiotherapy treatments per year", "Because basic insurance does not reimburse this physiotherapy, her reimbursement depends on the number of treatments in the supplementary insurance. Note acceptance and any waiting periods."], ["A reimbursement policy, so that basic insurance reimburses all physiotherapy", "A reimbursement policy also reimburses only care from the basic package; this physiotherapy falls outside it."], ["A voluntary deductible, so that the premium reduction covers the cost of the treatments", "A voluntary deductible lowers the premium, but does not reimburse physiotherapy that is not in the package."], ["Apply for the healthcare allowance, which is intended for physiotherapy costs", "The healthcare allowance is a contribution towards the premium, not towards particular healthcare costs."]], "2e.4"],
["How is the amount of the healthcare allowance calculated in essence?", [["Standard premium minus a standard contribution that depends on income", "The healthcare allowance is the difference between a set standard premium and the standard contribution that someone can bear himself on the basis of his income."], ["A fixed percentage of the premium actually paid for basic insurance", "The actual premium plays no role; the calculation is based on the standard premium."], ["The difference between the premium and the chosen deductible", "The deductible plays no role in the calculation of the healthcare allowance."], ["Last year's healthcare costs, divided by twelve", "The healthcare allowance does not depend on the healthcare costs incurred."]], "1g.6"],
["Lisa lives in one house with a friend. They are not partners, have no cohabitation agreement and no child together. Does that friend's income count for Lisa's healthcare allowance?", [["No, only the income of an allowance partner counts", "A housemate is not an allowance partner; for the healthcare allowance only the income of the applicant and any allowance partner counts."], ["Yes, the income of every housemate counts for the healthcare allowance", "Housemates play a role in the rent allowance, not in the healthcare allowance."], ["Yes, if they have been registered at the same address for longer than six months", "Without a partnership, cohabitation agreement or other partner criterion, the duration of registration does not make her an allowance partner."], ["Only if the friend herself does not receive a healthcare allowance", "Whether the friend herself receives an allowance does not make her an allowance partner."]], "1g.6"],
["At what moment are assets tested for the right to the healthcare allowance for a given year?", [["On 1 January of the year for which the healthcare allowance is requested", "For the assets test for allowances, the reference date is 1 January of the calculation year."], ["On 31 December of the year for which the healthcare allowance is requested", "The reference date is not the end but the beginning of the year."], ["On the day on which the application is submitted", "The moment of application does not determine the reference date."], ["On the average of the monthly balances over the year", "No annual average is taken; a single reference date applies."]], "1g.6"],
["Bram (25) lives alone in Groningen and receives the healthcare allowance based on the income from his part-time job. After graduating he gets a permanent job on 1 September with a clearly higher salary. He is healthy and has only basic insurance. He wonders whether he still has to arrange anything for his healthcare allowance. What must Bram do?", [["Report the change to the Benefits Administration within four weeks", "Changes that affect the allowance must be reported within four weeks, so that the advance is correct and repayment afterwards remains limited."], ["Nothing; the allowance is adjusted only after his income tax return", "Waiting for the tax return often leads to a high recovery; Bram must report the change himself."], ["Cancel his health insurance, because he no longer needs an allowance", "Health insurance is mandatory; a higher income only changes the amount of the allowance."], ["Ask his new employer to offset the allowance against his wages", "Employers do not offset the healthcare allowance; that runs through the Benefits Administration."]], "1j.3"],
["Someone disagrees with the decision on his healthcare allowance. Within what period can he lodge an objection?", [["Within six weeks of the date of the decision", "Under the General Administrative Law Act (Awb) a period of six weeks applies for an objection."], ["Within three months of the date of the decision", "Three months is longer than the objection period under the Awb."], ["Within a year, equal to the period for the application", "The application period and the objection period are different periods."], ["At any time, as long as the allowance has not been finally determined", "A fixed objection period applies against every decision."]], "1g.6"],
["Why can a health insurer predict the claims burden for a large group of insured persons better than for a single insured person?", [["Through the law of large numbers: the group average is highly predictable", "The larger the group, the smaller the relative deviation between expected and actual costs; this makes the premium calculation reliable."], ["Because every insured person in a large group incurs the same healthcare costs", "Individual costs continue to differ greatly; only the group average becomes predictable."], ["Because the government determines the claims burden of large groups in advance", "The government does not determine the claims burden; the predictability follows from the size of the group."], ["Because large groups consist mainly of healthy insured persons", "A large group in fact contains all kinds of risks; the predictability comes from the numbers, not from selection."]], "1e.1"],
["Why does an insurer take the average claim amount per insured person into account when calculating the risk premium?", [["The expected claims burden depends on the probability of a claim and the average size of the claim", "The risk premium is in essence the expected loss per insured person: the probability of a claim times the average claim amount."], ["Because every insured person is reimbursed exactly the average claim amount in the event of a claim", "The reimbursement depends on the actual costs, not on the average."], ["Because the law prescribes that the premium equals the highest claim", "No such prescription exists; the premium would then become far too high."], ["Because the average claim amount determines the adviser's remuneration", "The adviser's remuneration is independent of the average claim amount."]], "1e.2"],
["What does it mean for a client that his health insurance adviser holds an AFM licence?", [["The firm meets Wft requirements such as expertise and is under the supervision of the AFM", "When granting the licence, the AFM assesses whether the firm meets the statutory requirements; thereafter it exercises continuous supervision."], ["The AFM guarantees that every piece of advice from the adviser is correct in substance", "The AFM assesses and supervises, but does not vouch for every individual piece of advice."], ["In the event of wrong advice from the adviser, the client always has his loss reimbursed by the AFM", "The AFM does not compensate loss; for that the client can turn to the adviser and possibly Kifid."], ["The adviser may only advise on policies of one health insurer", "A licence does not determine with how many insurers an adviser works."]], "1f.11"],
["A health insurer wants to start working with a new advisory firm that is going to mediate its policies. What must the insurer in any case check beforehand?", [["Whether the firm holds a Wft licence to mediate in health insurance", "An insurer may do business only with an intermediary that holds the required licence or is exempt from it."], ["Whether the firm has made a profit in the past three years", "Profitability is not a statutory test that the insurer must carry out beforehand."], ["Whether all the firm's clients are already insured with the insurer", "That is not a condition for cooperation."], ["Whether the firm has a branch in every province", "The spread of branches is not relevant to the statutory obligations."]], "1f.9"],
["When is there double insurance?", [["When the same interest is insured against the same risk with more than one insurer", "Two policies then cover the same loss; the insured person has the loss reimbursed in total only once."], ["When the sum insured is clearly higher than the actual value of the insured interest", "That is called over-insurance, not double insurance."], ["When the sum insured is lower than the actual value of the insured interest", "That is called under-insurance."], ["When two partners each have their own basic insurance", "Each insures their own interest; there is no question of double insurance."]], "1i.12"],
["What does the principle of indemnity involve for a health insurance that reimburses costs incurred?", [["Reimbursement may not leave the insured person better off than before", "A non-life insurance reimburses at most the costs actually incurred; therefore the same invoice cannot be claimed in full from two insurers."], ["The insurer always pays a fixed amount, regardless of the actual costs", "A fixed amount belongs to fixed-sum insurance; indemnity in fact starts from the actual loss."], ["The insured person must pay half of every invoice himself", "That is not a principle of insurance law, but at most a policy condition."], ["The insurer may never take recourse against a liable third party", "Recourse fits precisely with the principle of indemnity, because in this way the insured person is not reimbursed twice."]], "1i.11"],
["Mrs Smits (84) has a Wlz assessment, but wants to keep living at home for as long as possible. Which forms of delivery are possible alongside residence in an institution?", [["Full package at home, modular package at home or a personal budget", "Alongside residence in an institution, the Wlz offers the full package at home (vpt), the modular package at home (mpt) and the personal budget (pgb), so that care can also be delivered at home."], ["Only district nursing under the Zvw and domestic help under the Wmo", "With a Wlz assessment she generally receives her care from the Wlz, even if she lives at home."], ["None; with a Wlz assessment admission to an institution is mandatory", "The Wlz in fact leaves room for care at home through various forms of delivery."], ["Only a one-off reimbursement for an adaptation to her home", "Home adaptation is a Wmo service and does not replace a Wlz form of delivery."]], "1i.1"],
["How is the Long-term Care Act mainly financed?", [["Through the national insurance contribution, levied with wage tax and income tax", "The Wlz is a national insurance; the contribution is levied on an income-related basis through payroll tax and income tax, supplemented by co-payments."], ["Through the nominal premium of basic insurance", "The nominal premium belongs to the Zvw, not to the Wlz."], ["Through municipal taxes, such as the property tax", "Municipal taxes do not finance the Wlz."], ["Through a fixed monthly premium that the care offices collect directly from all insured persons", "Care offices do not collect premium; the Wlz contribution is levied through the Tax Administration."]], "1c.3"],
["Which three functions does the application form have when a supplementary health insurance is concluded?", [["Offer to conclude the insurance, source of information for the risk assessment and evidence", "With the form the applicant makes an offer, the insurer obtains the data to assess the risk and what was disclosed is recorded."], ["Policy, premium invoice and proof of payment in one document", "The application form precedes the contract; the policy and premium invoice follow only after acceptance."], ["Cancellation of the old insurance, authorisation for direct debit and complaint form", "Those functions belong to other documents, not to the application form."], ["Permission from the AFM, registration with the CAK and application for the healthcare allowance", "An application form has nothing to do with the AFM, the CAK or the healthcare allowance."]], "1i.8"],
["What is meant by a non-cancellable health insurance?", [["The insurer may not terminate the insurance unilaterally", "With a non-cancellable policy the insured person can rely on his cover continuing, even if he incurs many costs."], ["The policyholder may never cancel the insurance again", "Non-cancellable refers to the insurer; the policyholder can cancel in accordance with the conditions."], ["The insurance can only be taken out through an adviser", "Non-cancellability says nothing about the distribution channel."], ["The insurance ends automatically after one year and must be renewed", "That is in fact the opposite of a non-cancellable insurance."]], "1k.5"],
["In which situation can an insurer nevertheless terminate a non-cancellable supplementary health insurance?", [["In the event of non-payment of the premium or fraud by the insured person", "Even a non-cancellable policy offers no protection in the case of non-payment or deliberate misleading of the insurer."], ["If the insured person incurs far more healthcare costs in a calendar year than average", "The claims record is in fact not a ground for terminating a non-cancellable policy."], ["If the insured person develops a chronic illness during the term", "Deteriorated health is not a ground for terminating a non-cancellable policy."], ["If the insurer lowers its premiums for new customers", "Premium policy for new customers is not a ground for cancellation."]], "1k.6"],
["Esra (29) is hit as a cyclist by a motorist who is liable. She is treated in hospital, and her health insurer pays the costs. What can the health insurer do afterwards?", [["Recover the healthcare costs paid from the motorist or his insurer", "For the reimbursed costs the health insurer steps into Esra's place (subrogation) and can take recourse against the liable party."], ["Oblige Esra to reclaim the costs from the motorist herself", "Recovering the reimbursed costs is a right of the insurer; Esra does not have to do this herself."], ["Still charge the costs to Esra, because someone else is liable", "Esra is insured; another person's liability does not affect her right to reimbursement."], ["Nothing, because healthcare costs can never be recovered from a liable third party", "A health insurer in fact has a right of recourse against the liable third party."]], "1l.9"],
["Sandra (32) has a serious mental illness and has just been discharged from a psychiatric clinic. She is temporarily unable to live independently and needs support. She has no lasting need for constant supervision or 24-hour care nearby. Her brother helps her look for somewhere to live. Where can Sandra generally turn for sheltered housing?", [["The municipality, under the Wmo", "Sheltered housing for people with mental health problems who have no lasting need for constant supervision falls under the Wmo."], ["The health insurer, under the basic insurance", "The Zvw reimburses treatment, but sheltered housing is social support provided by the municipality."], ["The care office, under the Wlz", "The Wlz is intended for those who permanently need constant supervision; that is not the case for Sandra."], ["The CAK, which assesses sheltered housing", "The CAK collects co-payments, but does not assess or arrange sheltered housing."]], "1i.1"],
["Jasper (17) lives with his mother in Almere and is in havo (senior general secondary education). He has been in treatment at a youth mental healthcare institution for an anxiety disorder for a year. In two months he turns 18, and the treatment will not yet be completed. His mother wonders who will pay for the treatment afterwards. What generally changes for the funding of his mental healthcare treatment?", [["From 18, his treatment falls under the Zvw instead of the Youth Act", "The Youth Act in principle applies up to age 18; thereafter mental healthcare treatment falls under basic insurance, with a deductible."], ["Nothing, because the Youth Act applies to mental healthcare up to age 27", "The Youth Act has no general limit of 27; mental healthcare treatment in principle passes to the Zvw at age 18."], ["From age 18 his treatment automatically falls under the Wlz", "The Wlz is only for those who permanently need constant supervision."], ["From age 18 he must pay for the treatment entirely himself", "The treatment remains insured, but now through the Zvw."]], "1i.1"],
["An insured person reports a claim under his supplementary insurance much later than the policy conditions prescribe. What is the consequence under insurance law as a rule?", [["The insurer can reduce the benefit by the prejudice it suffers because of the late notification", "Late notification does not automatically lead to loss of the right to a benefit; the insurer can, however, reduce it insofar as it has been prejudiced."], ["The right to a benefit always lapses, regardless of the consequences for the insurer", "Forfeiture of the right is possible only in special cases, such as intent to mislead or where the insurer's reasonable interest has been harmed."], ["No consequence at all, because notification periods in policy conditions are not binding", "Policy conditions are binding; late notification can have consequences for the benefit."], ["The entire insurance is dissolved retroactively", "Late notification of a claim does not lead to dissolution of the entire insurance."]], "1l.8"],
["What is sensible for an insured person who wants to have a planned operation carried out in a hospital in another EU country?", [["Ask his insurer beforehand about permission and reimbursement", "For planned care abroad, permission may be needed in advance and reimbursement is often limited; checking beforehand prevents surprises."], ["Simply go; the EHIC reimburses planned treatments throughout the EU in full", "The EHIC is intended for medically necessary care during a temporary stay, not for planned treatments."], ["First apply for an authorisation from the CIZ", "The CIZ assesses for the Wlz and does not decide on care abroad."], ["Take out travel insurance, because it fully covers planned operations abroad", "Travel insurance covers unexpected costs during trips, not planned treatments."]], "1g.7"],
["When is a policyholder entitled to a refund of premium under a health insurance?", [["If the insurance ends mid-term, for the period after the end date", "Premium is due only as long as the insurance runs; premium paid in advance for the period thereafter is refunded, for example on emigration or death."], ["If he has used no care in a calendar year", "A no-claims discount is not permitted in basic insurance."], ["If his deductible has not been used up at the end of the year", "The deductible is not a savings pot; not using it does not lead to a premium refund."], ["If he earns less in the course of the year", "A lower income may affect the healthcare allowance, not the premium."]], "1k.9"],
["During her holiday in France, Noor uses her EHIC with a doctor who is part of the French public system. Under what conditions does she receive care?", [["Under the conditions and tariffs of the French system, including co-payments", "With the EHIC the insured person receives care under the rules of the country of stay; co-payments that apply there may therefore be at her own expense."], ["Always completely free of charge, regardless of the French rules", "The EHIC does not guarantee free care; the rules and co-payments of the country of stay apply."], ["Under the conditions of her Dutch policy, at the tariffs that apply in the Netherlands", "When using the EHIC, the rules of the country of stay apply, not those of the Dutch policy."], ["Only if she has a supplementary insurance with worldwide cover", "The EHIC is linked to the basic insurance and requires no supplementary insurance."]], "1l.10"],
["Ahmed (39) is a project manager at a Dutch engineering firm and lives with his family in Amersfoort. Every year he works for a few months on projects in the United States and remains a resident of the Netherlands. He has only basic insurance. He wonders whether he needs to take extra measures for medical costs outside Europe. What is careful advice?", [["Consider travel or supplementary insurance; basic pays only the Dutch tariff", "In countries with high healthcare costs, such as the United States, the invoice can be far above the Dutch tariff; basic insurance does not cover that difference."], ["No extra measures; basic insurance always reimburses the full invoice worldwide", "Outside the Netherlands, basic insurance reimburses at most the tariff customary in the Netherlands."], ["Cancel his basic insurance and from now on take only a travel insurance", "As long as Ahmed is subject to the insurance obligation, he must keep a basic insurance."], ["Have himself registered with the CAK as a treaty beneficiary for the US", "Registration as a treaty beneficiary is intended for those who live abroad, not for a resident with temporary work elsewhere."]], "1l.11"],
["What must a health insurer do if a policyholder has an arrear of four monthly premiums?", [["Warn him that a report to the CAK follows at six months' arrears", "At four months of arrears the insurer warns that a report to the CAK will follow at an arrear of six monthly premiums."], ["Report him immediately to the CAK for an administrative-law premium", "Reporting to the CAK takes place only at an arrear of six monthly premiums."], ["Terminate the basic insurance and stop the cover", "The basic insurance may not be terminated for non-payment; the defaulters scheme in fact provides for continuing cover."], ["Engage a bailiff to immediately seize his home and wages", "A seizure of the home is not a step that the defaulters scheme prescribes at four months."]], "1a.2"],
["What role does a health insurer have in the early detection of debts by municipalities?", [["It reports payment arrears to the municipality so it can offer help", "Under the Municipal Debt Assistance Act, fixed-cost partners such as health insurers report arrears, so that the municipality can offer help early."], ["It decides itself whether the insured person enters debt restructuring", "The court, not the insurer, decides on admission to statutory debt restructuring."], ["It raises the premium of insured persons who already have debts", "Premium differentiation according to payment behaviour is not permitted in basic insurance."], ["None; the GDPR prohibits sharing payment data with municipalities", "There is a statutory basis for this exchange of data, so the GDPR does not prohibit it."]], "1c.9"],
["When does the CAK stop levying the administrative-law premium on a defaulter?", [["When the debt has been repaid or he takes part in a debt arrangement", "The administrative-law premium ends when the arrears have been paid or when the policyholder has an arrangement through a debt assistance programme."], ["Automatically after twelve months, regardless of the debt", "There is no fixed term; the premium continues until the conditions for ending it are met."], ["As soon as he switches to another health insurer", "With a premium arrear he cannot switch, and switching does not settle the debt."], ["When he takes out a supplementary insurance with the same insurer", "A supplementary insurance has no influence on the defaulters scheme."]], "1k.2"],
["Do the rules of the defaulters scheme also apply to the premium for children under 18 who are on the policy of a defaulter?", [["No, no premium is due for minors", "Minors pay no premium; the defaulters scheme concerns the premium of the policyholder and adult insured persons."], ["Yes, the children are also reported to the CAK and lose their cover", "Children do not lose their cover; no premium is due for them."], ["Yes, the parent pays an extra administrative-law premium for each child", "No administrative-law premium is levied for children."], ["No, but the children must switch to another health insurer", "A switch by the children is neither necessary nor mandatory."]], "1k.2"],
["A client is dissatisfied with the advice of his financial adviser on the choice of a health insurance. To which body can he turn with a complaint about the adviser after the internal complaints procedure?", [["Kifid (Dutch Financial Services Complaints Institute)", "Complaints about financial advisers and intermediaries belong to Kifid; the SKGZ deals with disputes with health insurers."], ["The SKGZ (Dutch Health Insurance Complaints and Disputes Foundation)", "The SKGZ settles disputes between insured persons and health insurers, not complaints about advisers."], ["The Dutch Healthcare Authority (NZa)", "The NZa does not handle individual complaints about financial advisers."], ["The National Health Care Institute", "The National Health Care Institute concerns the basic package, not complaints about advice."]], "1a.11"],
["How does an insurance contract, such as a supplementary health insurance, come into being?", [["By offer and acceptance; the policy is evidence", "An insurance contract is not subject to formal requirements and comes into being through offer and acceptance; the policy is evidence of the contract."], ["Only at the moment the first premium has been paid", "Payment of premium is an obligation under the contract, not a condition for its coming into being."], ["Only through signing of the policy before a notary", "No notarial deed is needed; the contract is not subject to formal requirements."], ["Only once the AFM has registered the contract", "The AFM does not register individual insurance contracts."]], "1i.5"],
["Which two routes does the SKGZ offer to an insured person with a problem with his health insurer?", [["Mediation by the Ombudsman and a ruling of the Disputes Committee", "The Ombudsman tries to mediate; if that fails, the Disputes Committee can issue a binding ruling."], ["A complaint to the AFM and then disciplinary proceedings before the medical disciplinary tribunal", "The AFM and the medical disciplinary tribunal are not part of the SKGZ."], ["An objection to the NZa and an appeal to the administrative court", "A dispute about a private-law health insurance does not proceed through an objection to the NZa."], ["A report to the CAK and a reassessment by the CIZ", "The CAK and CIZ are involved in the Wlz and Wmo, not in disputes with health insurers."]], "1a.11"],
["What is the nature of a ruling by the Health Insurance Disputes Committee?", [["A binding opinion, by which the insured person and the insurer are in principle bound", "The ruling is a binding opinion; a court can review it only to a limited extent."], ["A non-binding opinion that the health insurer may ignore", "The ruling is not non-binding; the health insurer is bound by it."], ["A judgment against which appeal lies to the court of appeal in the relevant region", "The Disputes Committee is not a court and does not issue judgments."], ["An administrative fine that the NZa imposes on behalf of the committee", "The Disputes Committee does not impose fines; it settles disputes."]], "1a.11"],
["A consumer wants to give a general signal about a health insurer that, in his view, systematically purchases too little care in his region. Which supervisor does that signal best suit?", [["The Dutch Healthcare Authority (NZa)", "The NZa supervises compliance with the duty of care by health insurers and collects signals about it."], ["The Dutch Data Protection Authority", "The Data Protection Authority concerns the processing of personal data, not care procurement."], ["The Netherlands Authority for the Financial Markets (AFM)", "The AFM exercises conduct supervision of financial services, not of the duty of care under the Zvw."], ["Kifid", "Kifid handles individual complaints about financial services, not signals about care procurement."]], "1a.3"],
["May an adviser receive commission from the health insurer for mediating in a health insurance?", [["Yes, no commission ban applies; the IDD conflict-of-interest rules do", "The commission ban applies, among other things, to mortgages and complex products; with health insurance, remuneration must not harm the client's interest."], ["No, since 2013 a full commission ban has applied to health insurance", "The 2013 commission ban does not apply to health insurance."], ["Only if the client waives his healthcare allowance in writing in advance", "The healthcare allowance has nothing to do with the adviser's remuneration."], ["Only if the NZa has approved the amount of the commission per policy", "The NZa does not approve advisers' commissions."]], "1f.2"],
["Mark (24) is healthy and wants to save premium by choosing the maximum voluntary deductible. What should the adviser in any case explain to him?", [["That he must be able to pay the full deductible if care is needed", "A higher deductible is sensible only if the client can find the amount when he unexpectedly needs care, for example after an accident."], ["That with a voluntary deductible he no longer has a right to GP care", "GP care remains insured and does not fall under the deductible."], ["That a voluntary deductible can be reduced back to zero only after five years", "The voluntary deductible can be adjusted annually."], ["That he then automatically no longer has a right to the healthcare allowance", "The voluntary deductible has no influence on the right to the healthcare allowance."]], "2e.6"],
["Which supervisor supervises the conduct of a financial adviser who advises on and mediates in health insurance?", [["The Netherlands Authority for the Financial Markets (AFM)", "The AFM exercises conduct supervision of financial service providers under the Wft, including when advising on health insurance."], ["The Dutch Healthcare Authority (NZa)", "The NZa supervises health insurers and care providers under the Zvw, not the conduct of financial advisers."], ["The Health and Youth Care Inspectorate (IGJ)", "The IGJ supervises the quality of care, not financial advice."], ["The National Health Care Institute", "The National Health Care Institute is not a conduct supervisor."]], "1f.7"],
["For health insurance, an adviser works with only two insurers. What must he tell the client before the insurance is concluded?", [["That it is not an impartial analysis, and which insurers he uses", "The IDD obliges the distributor to state whether his advice is based on an impartial analysis of the market; if not, he names the insurers."], ["Nothing; cooperation arrangements are commercially confidential information", "The client in fact needs to know on what basis the advice is produced."], ["That he is obliged to refer the client to an independent adviser", "He may advise himself, provided he is transparent about his way of working."], ["That the client must himself request the premiums of all other insurers", "The adviser may not place that responsibility on the client in this way; he must, however, be clear about his limited offering."]], "1f.17"],
["On what basis does an adviser process the name and address details of a client who instructs him to mediate in a health insurance?", [["Necessary for the performance of a contract", "These data are needed to carry out the assignment; the GDPR provides the basis of performance of a contract for this."], ["Vital interest of the data subject", "Vital interest is intended for life-threatening situations, not for mediating in an insurance."], ["Performance of a task carried out in the public interest", "That basis is intended for public tasks, not for commercial services."], ["No basis needed, because they are not special category personal data", "A basis is needed for every processing of personal data."]], "1a.14"],
["A client asks his adviser which personal data the firm holds about him. Within what period must the firm generally respond?", [["Within one month, extendable for complex requests", "The GDPR gives a period of one month, which can be extended by two months for complex requests or large numbers of requests."], ["Within 72 hours", "72 hours applies to reporting data breaches, not to access requests."], ["Within a year", "A year is far too long; the GDPR requires a prompt response."], ["The firm does not have to respond if the client gives no reason", "An access request does not have to be justified."]], "1a.13"],
["An advisory firm has its client records containing health information hosted by an external IT supplier. What must the firm in any case arrange under the GDPR?", [["A data processing agreement with the IT supplier", "A party that processes personal data on behalf of the firm is a processor; a data processing agreement must be concluded with it."], ["A licence from the AFM for the IT supplier", "The AFM does not grant licences to IT suppliers for data processing."], ["Permission from the Dutch Data Protection Authority for each client", "Permission from the Data Protection Authority for each client is not required."], ["Nothing, as long as the supplier is established in the Netherlands", "Even with a Dutch supplier, a data processing agreement remains necessary."]], "4a.3"],
["A client asks his intermediary to cancel his supplementary insurance because he wants a cheaper policy with another insurer. What should the intermediary in any case do?", [["Check that the new policy is accepted, so the client has no gap in cover", "For supplementary insurances there is no obligation to accept applicants and sometimes a waiting period; the intermediary prevents a gap in cover."], ["Send the cancellation immediately, because the client himself asks for it", "Carrying it out without checking can leave the client uninsured if the new insurer does not accept him."], ["Advise the client to cancel the basic insurance too without a new policy", "Without basic insurance the client would be acting in breach of the insurance obligation."], ["Refuse the cancellation, because cancelling is disadvantageous to the insurer", "The intermediary serves the client's interest, not that of the insurer."]], "1f.15"],
["May a financial adviser freely use a client's citizen service number (BSN) as a client number in his records?", [["No, the BSN may be used only if a law permits it", "The BSN is a statutory identification number; processing is permitted only insofar as a law prescribes or permits it."], ["Yes, if the client gives consent orally or in writing", "Consent is not a sufficient basis for the use of the BSN."], ["Yes, because the BSN is not personal data", "The BSN is personal data, even with extra protection."], ["Yes, as long as the file is well secured", "Security does not make use without a statutory basis permissible."]], "4a.3"],
["What does the client's own responsibility under the Wft involve, for example when taking out a health insurance?", [["The client must give correct and complete information and read the information provided", "Even if the adviser works carefully, the client remains responsible for correct data and for taking note of the information."], ["The client is himself liable for any wrong advice from his adviser", "The adviser remains responsible for the quality of his own advice."], ["The client must check the licence, otherwise the advice is invalid", "A client can consult the register, but the validity of advice does not depend on it."], ["The client must first compare all policies on the market himself before asking for advice", "That is precisely why he engages an adviser; it is not an obligation of the client."]], "1f.8"]
];
